━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Streams is facet of Checker
    sees Loops
    sees StateMachines

_ pattern-arms = PatternArms()
_ action-selects = false
_ remakes-result = false
_ outline-unsure = false

────────────────────
_ get buffer-item TypeId

` The type of the items the buffer of the stream a pattern reads holds: the stream's items, or
` bytes where it is `encoded`.
if stream-view.buffer != no-type then class-arg(types, stream-view.buffer, 0) else stream-view.item

────────────────────
_ get beside-rule Bool

` Whether the local rules being typed are those of a rule a module declares, beside its own
` pattern, rather than those of a match.
rule-streaming.matched == 0 && own-match != 0

.. own-match = rule-match(program, instances.rows[instance].module, instances.rows[instance].decl)

────────────────────
_ get own-helper Bool

` Whether the helper in force is the rule's own: the one this instance is typed for, or the one
` the rule is given as an argument.
rule-helper-site != 0 && helping.site == rule-helper-site

────────────────────
+ do type-helper Bool
    - helper SyntaxId

` Types the helper a stream match is given with `with`, after its subject, and resolves what it
` can do as the reference does, reporting there what the reference reports. One that can do
` nothing is reported; one that can is the helper of the match's pattern. One whose collector
` storages disagree, or that is no object, has no shape here. False where the match has no shape.
. type = infer(helper)
if type == invalid-type
    = false
if type == no-type
    decline(helper)
    = false
. resolved = pattern-helper(types, type)
if resolved.problem != null
    frame.diagnose(helper, .stated, program.store-atom(resolved.problem))
    = false
if !resolved.is-active
    frame.diagnose
        - helper
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("Pattern helper implements no pattern capability")
    = false
if resolved.storage == invalid-type || types.intrinsic-of(type) != .class
    decline(helper)
    = false
facts.set-plan(instance, helper, .plan-pattern-helper)
helping = helping.helper = resolved
helping = helping.site = helper
= true

────────────────────
+ do infer-stream-match TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - is-root Bool

` A stream pattern a match runs, typed over a stream of its own: a pattern around it, whose
` action holds the match, reads its own stream again after.
. buffer = stream-view
. result = infer-stream-pattern(id, pattern, is-root)
stream-view = buffer
= result

────────────────────
_ do infer-stream-pattern TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - is-root Bool

` A stream pattern a match runs on the String it is on. The String is read through a
` `TextTokenStream`, whose buffer holds its UTF-8 bytes, by calls the type pass records at the
` pattern, in the order `record-stream-protocol` makes them. Its arms are typed as the
` reference declares them and joined, and its value is optional unless its last arm always
` passes. Where an arm gives the text it matched, or an action reads it as `it`, the call
` that slices it from the stream's buffer is recorded there. A match that is returned has the
` type the function returns, as its arms do, even those that give an optional, or what that
` type holds where it is optional. One that always passes panics where the stream defers its last arm, which no stream a
` String is read through does. The names the pattern captures are typed before its arms. The
` match `if` or `while` tests a pattern with gives true where its arm ran, and false where
` none did.
if id != rule-streaming.matched
    = infer-scoped-pattern(id, pattern, is-root)
if matching.subject == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if is-root && !iterates(matching.subject) && natural-item(matching.subject) == no-type
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Can't convert to iterable"))
    = invalid-type
if !is-root || !record-stream-protocol(id, matching.subject)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. returned = facts.node-type(instance, id)
. target = no-type
if returned != no-type && returned != invalid-type
    target = if types.is-optional(returned) then types.optional-inner(returned) else returned
. result = type-stream-arms(pattern, true, target, target != returned)
if result == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if matching.open
    if result != types.bool-type
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-open)
    = result
if !always-passes(pattern)
    = types.optional-around(result)
instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
= result

────────────────────
_ do infer-scoped-pattern TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - is-root Bool

` A stream pattern written in the code of a function declared over the items of a stream, as
` the reference runs it: on the stream the function is given, from where the stream stands,
` through the calls a match on that stream records at the pattern. Its arms are typed and
` joined with no type to give but their own, and one that gives no value gives what its last
` part gives where that is optional, as the reference gives it. It gives an optional
` `CaptureResult` of the stream's items and what the arms give, which holds the items the
` pattern read beside that, and nothing where no arm passed. One in the code of a local rule
` runs on the stream the rule is called on, as `coded-rule-type` says. One in any other
` function is an error, and one in the arms of another pattern or under a helper has no shape
` here. Where the
` metrics of stream patterns compile, each result it gives is counted, as the reference counts it.
` A function or local rule a pattern on a String calls reads the stream's UTF-8 bytes, and its
` `CaptureResult` holds those bytes.
. stream = if rule-streaming.stream != no-type then rule-streaming.stream else scope-stream()
. texts = if rule-streaming.stream != no-type then rule-streaming.encoded else instances.rows[instance].encoded
if is-root || stream == no-type || rule-streaming.matched != 0 || helping.helper != null
    if stream == no-type && rule-streaming.matched == 0 && helping.helper == null
        frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(streamless-text))
    else
        decline(id)
    = invalid-type
    .. streamless-text = "This pattern has no stream to read; outside a rule, write it in a match whose arms are all ~ patterns"
. saved-rule = rule-streaming
rule-streaming = rule-streaming.stream = no-type
rule-streaming = rule-streaming.encoded = false
. own-matching = matching
. saved-body = helping
matching = matching.subject = stream
matching = matching.optional = false
matching = matching.closed = 0
matching = matching.arms = 0
matching = matching.open = false
matching = matching.rows = false
rule-streaming = rule-streaming.matched = id
helping = helping.body = id
. result = invalid-type
. item = no-type
if record-stream-protocol(id, stream, texts)
    item = buffer-item
    result = type-stream-arms(pattern, false)
else
    decline(id)
rule-streaming = rule-streaming.matched = 0
. carried-rolls = helping.rolls
helping = saved-body
helping = helping.rolls = carried-rolls
matching = own-matching
rule-streaming = saved-rule
if result == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if program.probes.compiles-metrics("stream-pattern")
    facts.record-call(instance, id, no-instance, .call-probe-metric, scratch.no-fills, false)
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(item)
scratch.types.push(result)
= types.optional-of
    - types.class-with-args(types.capture-result-decl.module, types.capture-result-decl.decl, mark)

────────────────────
_ do scope-stream TypeId

` The stream a function declared over the items of one is given, which a pattern written in
` its code runs on. None in a rule, whose pattern is its body, in a function written in
` another, and in any other function.
. row = instances.rows[instance]
if row.enclosing != no-instance || instances.signatures[instance].args.count == 0 || ruled
    = no-type
.. ruled = rule-match(program, row.module, row.decl) != 0
do match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        do match? program.modules[row.module].tree.nodes[fn.syntax]
            | .node-function-syntax(syntax)
                if syntax.pattern != 0 && !fn.is-generated
                    = instances.argument-type(instance, 0)
= no-type

────────────────────
+ do type-stream-arms TypeId
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - texts Bool
    - target TypeId = no-type
    - lifts Bool = true

` The arms of a stream pattern over the stream in force, typed as the reference declares them
` and joined: the names it captures first, then each arm, the text it matched where it gives
` no other value. Where the pattern `texts`, as the arms of a match, a pipe or a loop do, an arm
` that gives no value gives its text though its last part is optional; elsewhere the reference
` gives that part.
` The arms are converted to the `target` where one is given, and else to the type they join
` as; where an arm gives null or an optional and the target `lifts`, to the `target` as an
` optional, which null is absent of.
if !text-items() && !is-integer(stream-view.item)
    . site = class-error-site(pattern)
    if site == U32.max
        decline(pattern)
        = invalid-type
    if site != 0
        frame.diagnose
            - site
            - .stated
            - program.store-atom("Character patterns can only match character or integer items")
        = invalid-type
. own-arms = rule-arming
. base = capture-sites.length
rule-arming = RuleArms(target, false, false, texts, pattern, base, rule-arming.casting)
. joined = arms-type(pattern)
-= capture-sites[base .. < capture-sites.length]
-= capture-slots[base .. < capture-slots.length]
-= capture-accumulating[base .. < capture-accumulating.length]
-= capture-patterns[base .. < capture-patterns.length]
-= capture-repeats[base .. < capture-repeats.length]
rule-arming = own-arms
if joined == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
. result = if target != no-type then target else joined-text
    .. joined-text = if joined == no-type then types.string-type else joined
if lifts && target != no-type && joined-null && !types.is-optional(target)
    result = types.optional-of(target)
.. joined-null = types.is-optional(joined) || joined == types.null-type
convert-stream-arms(pattern, result)
facts.set-node-type(instance, pattern, result)
= result

────────────────────
+ do arms-type TypeId
    - pattern SyntaxId

` The arms of a stream pattern, typed after the names it captures and joined, with what
` `settle-captures` then records for those names, and what `results-assumed` settles of the
` actions that took their own type for the one the arms give, which is the one they declare
` or else join as, text where they give none. While they are typed, `pattern-arms` says whether
` an action or a call of this pattern makes a value through the helper (`selects`), which arm is
` being typed (`arm`), and that arms are scoped (`scoped`), each of which the
` reference gives a scope of its own, so that one name may hold another type in another arm.
` Where the arms declare no type and an action is `uninferred`, the reference
` takes that arm to give none, so the arms have a shape here only where they give text, which
` is what the reference takes them to give then. An arm that made the text it matched as the
` type its last part gives, taking that for the type the arms join as, has a shape only where
` they join as it.
. saved = pattern-arms
pattern-arms = pattern-arms.selects = false
pattern-arms = pattern-arms.uninferred = false
pattern-arms = pattern-arms.scoped = true
pattern-arms = pattern-arms.arm = 0
pattern-arms = pattern-arms.joined = tree.nodes[pattern] is .node-stream-or
. assumed = assumed-results.length
. sourced = assumed-sources.length
. joined = if type-captures(pattern, 0) then stream-arm-type(pattern) else invalid-type
note-observed(pattern)
for position in sourced .. < assumed-sources.length
    if joined != invalid-type && assumed-sources[position] != joined
        decline(pattern)
        joined = invalid-type
-= assumed-sources[sourced .. < assumed-sources.length]
if joined != invalid-type && !settle-captures(pattern, settled-target)
    joined = invalid-type
.. settled-target = if rule-arming.target != no-type then rule-arming.target else joined
if joined == invalid-type
    -= assumed-results[assumed .. < assumed-results.length]
else if !results-assumed(assumed, if targeted then rule-arming.target else joined-text, pattern)
    joined = invalid-type
.. targeted = rule-arming.target != no-type
.. joined-text = if joined == no-type then types.string-type else joined
if pattern-arms.uninferred && joined != invalid-type && joined != no-type && joined != types.string-type
    decline(pattern)
    joined = invalid-type
pattern-arms = saved
= joined

────────────────────
_ do top-arm SyntaxId
    - node SyntaxId

` The arm of the pattern being typed that a node lies in, or none. The nodes of an arm lie
` together, though those of the alternatives that join the arms do not.
. arms [SyntaxId]
stream-arms(rule-arming.capture-root, arms)
for arm in arms
    if tree.subtree-start(arm) <= node && node <= arm
        = arm
= 0

────────────────────
_ do enter-arm
    - id SyntaxId

` Begins typing an arm of the pattern: each name the arm captures has the type its place in
` this arm gave it.
pattern-arms = pattern-arms.arm = id
if !pattern-arms.scoped
    =
for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-sites.length
    . site = capture-sites[position]
    if tree.subtree-start(id) <= site && site <= id
        frame.assign(capture-slots[position], facts.node-type(instance, site))

────────────────────
_ do optional-operand SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

` The part an optional part of a stream pattern holds, or none for any other part.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        if row.op == .zero-or-one-op
            = row.operand
= 0

────────────────────
_ do optional-text Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a name captured over the text a part of a stream pattern matched may hold none, as
` the reference types it: where the part is optional, or alternatives one of which is. A
` sequence holds the text it matched, though the part it ends with may be optional.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        = row.op == .zero-or-one-op
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        = optional-text(row.left) || optional-text(row.right)
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = optional-text(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && tree.lazies-only(row.right) && optional-text(row.pattern)
= false

────────────────────
_ do settle-captures Bool
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - result TypeId

` Records what the reference makes through the helper where a part a name captures passes,
` whether or not anything reads it, once the arms are typed. An optional part captured as a
` whole that gives its text makes it, as the type it holds, but for one literal, whose text
` the reference has as a constant, and one of text that actions read, but none for more than
` its length, which the reference keeps as the span it matched. Where no action or call of the
` pattern makes a value through the helper, a call of a rule that gives its text makes it
` too, as the type the rule states, but for one whose name the reference keeps as the span
` it matched: a name that holds text, so captured outside optional parts and repeats, and
` does not accumulate. Each is made by the capture materializer `record-eager` selects, and
` nothing where the helper has none. There, a call in a repeat that states another type
` than text, a name an action reads for more than its length, a sequence that ends with
` such a call, a count whose bounds are computed, and a helper that delegates what makes the
` type the arms give have no shape here. False where the pattern was declined.
if helping.helper == null || helping.helper.captures.length == 0
    = true
for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-sites.length
    . name = capture-sites[position]
    . part = capture-patterns[position]
    if facts.plan-of(instance, name) == .plan-stream-value
        continue
    . held = facts.node-type(instance, name)
    if optional-operand(part) != 0
        if capture-accumulating[position] || literal-part || sourceless
            continue
        .. literal-part = tree.nodes[optional-operand(part)] is .node-stream-string
        .. sourceless = source-candidates(peeled-optional(held)).length == 0
        if held == types.optional-of(types.string-type) && read-in && !plain-read
            continue
        .. read-in = reads-slot-in(pattern, capture-slots[position])
        .. plain-read = reads-plainly(pattern, capture-slots[position])
        if !pattern-arms.selects && delegates-result(result)
            decline(name)
            = false
        if !record-eager(part, peeled-optional(held))
            = false
        continue
    if pattern-arms.selects
        continue
    . called = closing-call(part)
    if called == 0
        continue
    . stated = facts.node-type(instance, called)
    if source-candidates(stated).length == 0 || made-at(called, .material-text)
        continue
    if called != part || computed-counts(pattern) || delegates-result(result) || reads-wide
        decline(name)
        = false
    .. reads-wide = reads-plainly(pattern, capture-slots[position])
    if stated == types.string-type && held == types.string-type && !capture-accumulating[position]
        continue
    if stated != types.string-type && is-listed(held)
        decline(name)
        = false
    if !record-eager(part, stated)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do record-eager Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - held TypeId

` Records at a part of a stream pattern the call of the capture materializer that makes a
` type of the text the part matched, as the reference's implicit materialization selects it
` among those that make that type from the stream's items, which the part makes where it
` passes. Nothing where the helper has none. False where the part has no shape, as one over
` items that are not characters has none.
. candidates = source-candidates(held)
if candidates.length == 0
    = true
if !text-items()
    decline(site)
    = false
. interface = select-materializer(candidates, buffer-item, held, true, site)
if interface == invalid-type
    = false
if interface == no-type
    = true
= record-material(site, .material-eager, no-slot, second-type-arg(interface), interface, no-type)

────────────────────
_ do closing-call SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

` The call of a rule that gives its text which a part of a stream pattern is, or which the
` sequence it is ends with, or none.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-call
        = if facts.plan-of(instance, id) == .plan-span-call then id else 0
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = closing-call(row.right)
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = closing-call(row.pattern)
= 0

────────────────────
_ do made-at Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - kind MaterialKind

` Whether the helper makes a value of a kind at a place, as recorded so far.
. row = facts.first-material(instance, site)
while row != U32.max
    if facts.materials[row].kind == kind
        = true
    row = facts.materials[row].next
= false

────────────────────
_ do computed-counts Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a stream pattern holds a count of a part whose bounds are not numbers written.
for node in tree.subtree-start(id) .. < id + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-stream-length(row)
            if !count-bound(row.min) || (row.max != 0 && !count-bound(row.max))
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do delegates-result Bool
    - result TypeId

` Whether a materializer that makes what a type holds, past optionals and lists, answers for
` the helper through a property the helper delegates it to.
. leaf = if result != no-type && result != invalid-type then desired-leaf(result) else no-type
for materializer in helping.helper!.captures
    if second-type-arg(materializer) == leaf && capability-receiver(helping.helper!.participant, materializer) != helping.helper!.participant
        = true
for materializer in helping.helper!.values
    if second-type-arg(materializer) == leaf && capability-receiver(helping.helper!.participant, materializer) != helping.helper!.participant
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do reads-slot-in Bool
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId

` Whether an action of a stream pattern reads a name.
for node in tree.subtree-start(pattern) .. < pattern + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-stream-transform(row)
            if row.right != 0 && !tree.lazies-only(row.right) && reads-slot(row.right, slot)
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do reads-plainly Bool
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId

` Whether an action of a stream pattern reads a name for more than its length, through `.` or,
` for an optional name, `?.`.
for node in tree.subtree-start(pattern) .. < pattern + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-stream-transform(row)
            if row.right != 0 && slot-read && !reads-length-only(slot, row.right) && wide-optional
                = true
            .. slot-read = !tree.lazies-only(row.right) && reads-slot(row.right, slot)
            .. wide-optional = !reads-length-only(slot, row.right, true)
= false

────────────────────
_ do type-captures Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - depth U32
    - repeats U32 = 0
    - held Bool = false

` Types the names a stream pattern captures, as the reference's matchmaker types them: each
` the text its part matched, or what a rule the part calls gives, optional within an optional
` part, and within a repeat an `ImmutableArray` of what each pass captured. A name captured in
` more than one place keeps one type, and its places must be alternatives of one another, so
` that no way through the pattern passes two of them; a name may hold another type in
` another arm, though, as the reference gives each arm a scope of its own, but for one
` captured in a repeat. A name captured in a lookahead,
` optional twice over, or in a repeat but for text no optional part holds, has no shape here,
` nor has any name but one that accumulates where `held`. A name that accumulates is typed
` wherever it is captured but in a count, whose names the reference never declares. A name
` captured over a call of a rule that gives its text but states another type has that type,
` and holds the text until an action makes it so: under a helper, optional where the call or
` a part around it is, and in one repeat a list that keeps the range of each pass. Records
` where each name holds text the call that makes it, and for one in a repeat the calls that
` grow its lists; plans each that holds a rule's value so. A name captured over a sequence
` that ends by testing an item against a value has no shape here: the reference converts the
` text the sequence matched to the value's type. False where the pattern was declined.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        if row.accumulating
            = type-accumulating(id, row.name, row.pattern)
        . inner = stream-node-type(row.pattern)
        if inner == invalid-type
            = false
        . slot = capture-slot(row.name)
        if held
            decline(id)
            = false
        for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-sites.length
            if capture-slots[position] == slot && capture-accumulating[position]
                frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Capture ${name-text(row.name)} mixes ordinary and accumulating capture modes"))
                = false
        . valued = stream-valued(row.pattern) || takes-item(row.pattern)
        . optional = types.optional-of(types.string-type)
        if !valued && inner == optional && !optional-text(row.pattern)
            inner = types.string-type
        . type = if depth != 0 then optional else inner
        if valued
            type = if depth != 0 then types.optional-of(inner) else inner
        . shapeless = if !valued then text-mismatch else (depth != 0 && types.is-optional(inner))
            .. text-mismatch = inner != types.string-type && (inner != optional || depth != 0)
        . sliced = !text-items() && !valued && pattern-spans && !holds-count(row.pattern)
            .. pattern-spans = returns-span(instance, row.pattern)
        . whole = optional-operand(row.pattern)
        . spanned = textless-inner && facts.plan-of(instance, planned-part) == .plan-span-call
            .. textless-inner = !valued && peeled-optional(inner) != types.string-type
            .. planned-part = if whole != 0 then whole else row.pattern
        if spanned && whole != 0
            type = inner
            shapeless = depth != 0 || repeats != 0 || helping.helper == null || whole-optional
                .. whole-optional = types.is-optional(facts.node-type(instance, whole))
        else if spanned && repeats != 0
            type = listed-type(repeats, inner)
            shapeless = depth != 0 || repeats != 1 || helping.helper == null || inner-optional
                .. inner-optional = types.is-optional(inner)
        else if spanned
            type = if depth != 0 then types.optional-of(inner) else inner
            shapeless = depth != 0 && (helping.helper == null || types.is-optional(inner))
        else if sliced
            type = stream-view.buffer
            shapeless = depth != 0 || repeats != 0
        else if !text-items() && !valued
            shapeless = true
        else if repeats != 0
            shapeless = depth != 0 || valued-optional || !(valued || inner == types.string-type)
                .. valued-optional = valued && types.is-optional(inner)
            type = listed-type(repeats, if valued then inner else types.string-type)
        if slot == no-slot || depth > 1 || shapeless || (valued && sequence-tests-item(row.pattern))
            decline(id)
            = false
        for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-sites.length
            if capture-slots[position] == slot
                . known = facts.node-type(instance, capture-sites[position])
                . apart = pattern-arms.scoped && other-arm && unrepeated && repeats == 0
                    .. other-arm = top-arm(capture-sites[position]) != top-arm(row.name)
                    .. unrepeated = capture-repeats[position] == 0
                if !alternatives(capture-sites[position])
                    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Capture ${name-text(row.name)} is captured twice on one way through the pattern"))
                    = false
                if known != type && !apart
                    . shown = "${type-short-name(types, known)} in one alternative and ${type-short-name(types, type)} in another"
                    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Capture ${name-text(row.name)} holds $shown"))
                    = false
        if valued
            facts.set-plan(instance, row.name, .plan-stream-value)
            if takes-item(row.pattern)
                facts.set-node-type(instance, row.pattern, inner)
            if repeats != 0 && !record-collectors(row.name, repeats, inner)
                decline(id)
                = false
        else if sliced
            facts.set-plan(instance, row.name, .plan-stream-slice)
        else if !record-stream-text(row.name)
            decline(id)
            = false
        else
            . ranged = spanned && repeats != 0
            if !ranged && repeats != 0 && helping.helper != null
                . found = ranged-capture(id, slot)
                if found == null
                    = false
                ranged = found
            . item = if ranged then types.pattern-capture-range-type else types.string-type
            if ranged && repeats != 1
                decline(id)
                = false
            if !record-collectors(row.name, repeats, item)
                decline(id)
                = false
            if ranged
                facts.record-material
                    - MaterialFact
                        - instance
                        - row.name
                        - .material-ranges
                        - slot
                        - class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, item)
                        - no-type
                        - no-fact
        frame.assign(slot, type)
        facts.set-node-type(instance, row.name, type)
        capture-sites += row.name
        capture-slots += slot
        capture-accumulating += false
        capture-patterns += row.pattern
        capture-repeats += repeats
        = type-captures(row.pattern, depth, repeats)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = type-captures(row.left, depth, repeats, held) && type-captures(row.right, depth, repeats, held)
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        if !type-captures(row.left, depth, repeats, held)
            = false
        right-arms += id
        . passes = type-captures(row.right, depth, repeats, held)
        right-arms.pop()
        = passes
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = type-captures(row.pattern, depth, repeats, held)
    | .node-stream-panic(row)
        = type-captures(row.pattern, depth, repeats, held)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        if row.op == .zero-or-one-op
            = type-captures(row.operand, depth + 1, repeats, held)
        . repeat = row.op == .zero-or-more-op || row.op == .one-or-more-op
        if repeat && depth == 0 && !held && listable(row.operand, row.operand)
            = type-captures(row.operand, 0, repeats + 1)
        = type-captures(row.operand, depth, repeats, true)
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        = captures-none(row.operand)
= true

────────────────────
_ do type-accumulating Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - name SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId

` Types a name that accumulates what its part gives each time the part passes, wherever it
` is captured, as the reference types one: an `ImmutableArray` of what the part gives, the
` text it matched or what a rule it calls gives, which every place that captures the name
` must give alike. Records where the part gives text the call that makes it, and the call
` that grows the list the match keeps of them. A name captured both so and plainly is
` TypeScript's error at the later place, as is a part that gives another type than the first.
` One over items that are not characters, or whose part gives an optional, has no shape here.
. inner = stream-node-type(pattern)
if inner == invalid-type
    = false
. slot = capture-slot(name)
if slot == no-slot
    decline(id)
    = false
. text = name-text(name)
for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-sites.length
    if capture-slots[position] == slot && !capture-accumulating[position]
        frame.diagnose
            - id
            - .stated
            - program.store-atom("Capture $text mixes ordinary and accumulating capture modes")
        = false
. valued = stream-valued(pattern)
if !text-items() || types.is-optional(inner) || (!valued && inner != types.string-type)
    decline(id)
    = false
. list = class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, inner)
for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-sites.length
    if capture-slots[position] == slot
        . first = facts.node-type(instance, capture-sites[position])
        if first != list
            . given = class-arg(types, first, 0)
            frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Accumulating capture $text has incompatible contribution types ${type-key(types, given)} and ${type-key(types, inner)}"), given, inner)
            = false
        break
if valued
    facts.set-plan(instance, name, .plan-stream-value)
else if !record-stream-text(name)
    decline(id)
    = false
if !record-collectors(name, 1, inner)
    decline(id)
    = false
frame.assign(slot, list)
facts.set-node-type(instance, name, list)
capture-sites += name
capture-slots += slot
capture-accumulating += true
capture-patterns += pattern
capture-repeats += 0
= type-captures(pattern, 0, 0, true)

────────────────────
_ name-text String
    - id SyntaxId

if name then name.text else ""

.. name = identifier-name(tree, id)

────────────────────
_ do accumulates Bool
    - slot SlotId

` Whether a name the match captures accumulates what its parts give.
for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-slots.length
    if capture-slots[position] == slot
        = capture-accumulating[position]
= false

────────────────────
_ capture-slot SlotId
    - name SyntaxId

if resolution.kind == .resolve-slot then resolution.slot else no-slot

.. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, name)

────────────────────
_ do alternatives Bool
    - earlier SyntaxId

` Whether a place a name was captured lies in an alternative tried before one the pattern is
` being typed in, so that no way through the pattern passes both.
for arm in right-arms
    do match? tree.nodes[arm]
        | .node-stream-or(row)
            if earlier >= tree.subtree-start(row.left) && earlier <= row.left
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do listed-type TypeId
    - repeats U32
    - item TypeId

` The type of a name captured in repeats nested this deep: an `ImmutableArray` of what each
` pass captured, the text or the item, for each.
. type = item
for level in 0 .. < repeats
    type = class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, type)
= type

────────────────────
_ do record-collectors Bool
    - name SyntaxId
    - repeats U32
    - first TypeId

` Records at a name captured in repeats nested this deep the call that grows the list each
` repeat keeps of what its passes captured, from the innermost out: a `PatternCollector` of
` what one pass captured, the text or the item, then of the lists the repeat inside it made.
. item = first
for level in 0 .. < repeats
    . collector = collector-over(item)
    if collector == invalid-type
        = false
    if calls.protocol-call(collector, program.store-atom("grow"), name).answer != grown-items(collector)
        = false
    item = class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, item)
= true

────────────────────
_ do collector-over TypeId
    - item TypeId

` The `PatternCollector` a stream pattern keeps a list of items of a type in, as the
` reference makes it: backed as the helper of the pattern keeps collectors, which the body
` then reads the context of where it makes one, and else by the collector. A match without
` such a helper in a rule whose own helper keeps collectors has no shape here, and the rule
` is typed for its helper so that the call of it has none either.
. decl = types.pattern-collector-decl
if decl.module == 0
    = invalid-type
. backing = types.gc-backing-type
if helping.helper != null && helping.helper.storage != no-type
    if !note-storage()
        = invalid-type
    backing = helping.helper!.storage
else if rule-helper-site != 0 && helping.site != rule-helper-site && rule-stores()
    instances.rows[instance].uses-helper = true
    = invalid-type
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(item)
scratch.types.push(backing)
= types.class-with-args(decl.module, decl.decl, mark)

────────────────────
_ do grown-items TypeId
    - collector TypeId

` The `Array` a `PatternCollector` keeps its items in: of its item, with its backing.
. item = class-arg(types, collector, 0)
. backing = class-arg(types, collector, 1)
if backing == types.gc-backing-type
    = class-over(types.array-decl, item)
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(item)
scratch.types.push(backing)
= types.class-with-args(types.array-decl.module, types.array-decl.decl, mark)

────────────────────
_ do note-storage Bool

` Notes that the body being typed keeps the items of its collectors where the helper says:
` the property read from the helper for the context, which answers `pattern-collector-context`
` for it, is recorded once, at the body, with the getter that answers it where the helper
` stores none, after the properties the helper delegates its collector storage through. A rule
` typed for the helper uses it so. False where the body or the property has no shape here.
if helping.body == 0 || helping.helper!.storage == invalid-type
    = false
if facts.storage-body-of(instance, helping.body) == U32.max
    . participant = helping.helper!.participant
    . receiver = capability-receiver(helping.helper!.participant, helping.helper!.storages[0])
    . places [U32]
    if receiver == no-type || (receiver != participant && !calls.ranking.delegate-path(participant, receiver, places))
        = false
    . found = property-named(receiver, program.store-atom("pattern-collector-context"))
    if !found
        = false
    . property = types.properties[found]
    if property.type == no-type || property.type == invalid-type
        = false
    places += found as U32
    . steps = facts.keep-steps(places, calls.step-getters(places, helping.body))
    facts.add-storage-body(StorageBody(instance, helping.body, steps, property.type))
note-helper-use(false)
= true

────────────────────
_ do rule-stores Bool

` Whether the helper a rule this instance types is given keeps collectors where it says.
. given = instances.rows[instance].helper
if given == no-type
    . position = ambient-position(types, instances, instance)
    if position == U32.max
        = false
    given = instances.argument-type(instance, position)
= pattern-helper(types, given).storage != no-type

────────────────────
_ do listable Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - operand SyntaxId

` Whether the names a repeat's part captures can be kept as lists: each is captured on every
` way the part passes, and the part runs no action. A name that accumulates keeps no list.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        if row.accumulating
            = listable(row.pattern, operand)
        . slot = capture-slot(row.name)
        = slot != no-slot && covers(operand, slot) && listable(row.pattern, operand)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = listable(row.left, operand) && listable(row.right, operand)
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        = listable(row.left, operand) && listable(row.right, operand)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        = listable(row.operand, operand)
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        = listable(row.operand, operand)
    | .node-stream-transform
        = false
    | .node-stream-panic
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do holds Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId

` Whether a part of a pattern captures a name anywhere in it.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = capture-slot(row.name) == slot || holds(row.pattern, slot)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = holds(row.left, slot) || holds(row.right, slot)
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        = holds(row.left, slot) || holds(row.right, slot)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        = holds(row.operand, slot)
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        = holds(row.operand, slot)
= false

────────────────────
_ do first-capture SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

` The first name a part of a pattern captures, or none.
for node in tree.subtree-start(id) .. < id + 1
    if tree.nodes[node] is .node-stream-capture
        = node
= 0

────────────────────
_ do captures-none Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - quiet Bool = false

` Whether a part of a pattern captures no name, declining the first that does where it is not
` `quiet`.
for node in tree.subtree-start(id) .. < id + 1
    if tree.nodes[node] is .node-stream-capture
        if !quiet
            decline(node)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do is-capture Bool
    - slot SlotId

for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-slots.length
    if capture-slots[position] == slot
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do covers Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId

` Whether a pattern gives a name the match captures a value on every way it passes. An
` optional part gives the names in it nothing where it does not pass; a repeat gives each a
` list, empty where it took its part no time.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = capture-slot(row.name) == slot || covers(row.pattern, slot)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = covers(row.left, slot) || covers(row.right, slot)
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        = covers(row.left, slot) && covers(row.right, slot)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        if row.op == .zero-or-more-op || row.op == .one-or-more-op
            = holds(row.operand, slot)
        = row.op == .zero-or-one-op && covers(row.operand, slot)
= false

────────────────────
_ do uncovered-read SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` Where an action reads a name the match captures that may hold no value on some way the
` action's pattern passes, or none where each holds one: the reference leaves one that an
` alternative not taken captures unset. A name that accumulates always holds its list. A
` function the action makes reads only names that hold one value each, as `reads-captures`
` says, and is where it reads another.
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier
            . slot = capture-slot(node)
            if slot != no-slot && is-capture(slot) && !accumulates(slot) && !covers(pattern, slot)
                = node
        | .node-function-syntax
            if capture-sites.length != rule-arming.capture-base && reads-captures(node)
                = node
= 0

────────────────────
_ uncovered-text String
    - read SyntaxId

` The error for an action that reads a name some way its pattern passes doesn't capture.
"Capture ${name-text(read)} holds no value on some ways this arm matches; capture it in every alternative"

────────────────────
_ slice-read-text String

` The error for a name captured as a slice of a stream that holds no characters, read for more
` than its length or an item.
"A capture over items that aren't characters can only be read for its length or an item"

────────────────────
_ do unplain-slice SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` Where an action reads a name captured as a slice of a stream that holds no characters for
` more than its length or an item of it, or none. The reference types the name as an
` `ImmutableArray` but gives it the `Array` it reads, which shares the stream's buffer, and the
` two agree only there.
. receivers [SyntaxId]
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-get-expression(row)
            if row.name == types.length-atom! && !row.is-optional
                receivers += row.object
        | .node-index-expression(row)
            if !row.is-optional
                receivers += row.object
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    if tree.nodes[node] is .node-identifier
        . slot = capture-slot(node)
        if slot != no-slot && is-capture(slot) && sliced && receivers.find(node) == null
            = node
        .. sliced = facts.plan-of(instance, bindings.slots[slot].syntax) == .plan-stream-slice
= 0

────────────────────
_ do reads-captures Bool
    - function SyntaxId

` Whether a function an action makes reads a name the match captures that holds more than the
` one value the function takes as it is made: one that collects what its parts give, or any
` under a helper, which makes the action's values. The binder records what the function reads
` of the function around it; one it kept no record of is taken to.
. row = bindings.bindings[frame.binding]
for offset in 0 .. < row.nested.count
    . nested = bindings.nested[row.nested.start + offset]
    if nested.syntax == function
        for index in 0 .. < nested.captures.count
            . slot = bindings.captures[nested.captures.start + index].slot
            if is-capture(slot) && (helping.helper != null || collects(slot))
                = true
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do collects Bool
    - slot SlotId

` Whether a name the match captures collects what its parts give: one that accumulates, or one
` written inside a repeat.
for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-slots.length
    if capture-slots[position] == slot && gathers
        = true
    .. gathers = capture-accumulating[position] || capture-repeats[position] != 0
= false

────────────────────
_ do outlines Bool
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - value TypeId

` Whether the reference runs an action in a function of its own, `stream-action`, which a
` panic in it would show: one with a pattern, whose value is not String and holds no function,
` in a function with no type parameters, a rule's own item type aside, that is more than a
` name, a number or text written alone, makes no function, and reads no local of the
` functions it is in but the names its match captures, `it` and `location`, none of which
` holds a function. The reference asks some of this by the names the action reads, so for an
` action that reads a name a local of its function also has the answer is not sure, which
` `outline-unsure` says. An action that names `This` is kept inline, as the reference finds
` no such type in the module.
outline-unsure = false
if pattern == 0 || value == types.string-type || trivial-action(body)
    = false
. params = instances.signatures[instance].param-count
. item-params = if rule-match(program, module, frame.decl) != 0 then 1u32 else 0u32
if params > item-params
    = false
if holds-function(value)
    = false
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-function-syntax
            = false
        | .node-type-identifier(row)
            if types.this-atom && row.name == types.this-atom
                = false
        | .node-identifier(row)
            if types.this-atom && row.name == types.this-atom
                = false
            . slot = capture-slot(node)
            . declared = bindings.slots[slot] if slot != no-slot
            . inside = declared && declared.syntax >= body-start && declared.syntax <= body
                .. body-start = tree.subtree-start(body)
            if !declared || inside
                if named-before(row.name, body)
                    outline-unsure = true
            else if declared.kind == .slot-it || declared.kind == .slot-location || is-capture(slot)
                if holds-function(frame.slot-type(slot))
                    = false
            else
                = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do trivial-action Bool
    - body SyntaxId

` Whether an action is a name, a number or text written alone, which the reference keeps
` inline.
. single = body
do match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-block(row)
        if row.body.count != 1
            = false
        single = tree.children[row.body.start]
do match? tree.nodes[single]
    | .node-identifier
        = true
    | .node-integer-syntax
        = true
    | .node-float-syntax
        = true
    | .node-string-syntax
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do named-before Bool
    - name Atom
    - body SyntaxId

` Whether a local of the function an action is in has a name: one declared before the
` action, in a scope the action is in.
. bound = bindings.bindings[frame.binding]
. start = tree.subtree-start(body)
for offset in 0 .. < bound.slots.count
    . other = bindings.slots[bound.slots.start + offset]
    if other.name != name || other.syntax >= start
        continue
    . held = bindings.scopes[other.scope].syntax
    if held == 0 || (tree.subtree-start(held) <= start && body <= held)
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do holds-function Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether a type holds a function anywhere in it: a closure, a binding or a function type, or a
` field, case, argument or property of one that does.
. seen [TypeId]
. waiting [TypeId]
waiting += type
while waiting.length != 0
    . next = waiting[waiting.length - 1]
    waiting.pop()
    if next == no-type || next == invalid-type || seen.find(next) != null
        continue
    seen += next
    do match? types.rows[next]
        | .type-closure
            = true
        | .type-binding
            = true
        | .type-function
            = true
        | .type-tuple(row)
            for position in 0 .. < row.fields.count
                waiting += types.child-type(row.fields, position)
        | .type-union(row)
            for position in 0 .. < row.cases.count
                waiting += types.child-type(row.cases, position)
        | .type-named-union(row)
            for position in 0 .. < row.cases.count
                waiting += types.child-type(row.cases, position)
        | .type-class(row)
            for position in 0 .. < row.args.count
                waiting += types.child-type(row.args, position)
            for property in types.properties-of(next)
                waiting += property.type
= false

────────────────────
_ do note-outlined-action
    - arm SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - it-type TypeId

` Records an action the reference runs in a function of its own, with the names it gives the
` function: `location`, `it` and the names the match captures, in the order the action first
` reads them, each of the type the arm gives it, which a helper may have made another.
. start U32 = facts.action-slots.length as U32
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier
            . slot = capture-slot(node)
            . type = no-type
            if slot != no-slot
                . row = bindings.slots[slot]
                if row.kind == .slot-location && row.syntax == arm
                    type = types.match-location-type
                else if row.kind == .slot-it && row.syntax == arm
                    type = it-type
                else if is-capture(slot)
                    type = frame.known(slot)
            . known = false
            for position in start .. < facts.action-slots.length
                known = known || facts.action-slots[position] == slot
            if type != no-type && !known
                facts.action-slots.append(slot)
                facts.action-types.append(type)
. count U32 = (facts.action-slots.length - start) as U32
facts.outlined.append
    - OutlinedAction(instance, arm, RowRange'U32(start, count), no-type, outline-unsure)

────────────────────
+ do record-stream-protocol Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - subject TypeId
    - encoded Bool = false

` Records at a stream pattern the calls the reference makes to run it on the value a match is
` on, in order: the stream it reads the value through, the stream's `pattern-view`, its
` `pattern-commit` of where the pattern ended and how far it read, and its `pattern-extend`. What a value is is what it
` is `supported` as. A value that is a stream
` is read as the `TokenStream` it is, converted to that interface, through the view of its
` UTF-8 bytes where it is a `TextTokenStream` or the stream given to a function a pattern on a
` String calls, which is `encoded`. A String is read through a `TextTokenStream` of
` it, whose buffer holds its UTF-8 bytes. A generator is read
` through a `ChunkedTokenStream` of its items, which pulls them as the pattern needs them. So
` is a stream of items a parameter is written as, `<T>`, which the reference passes as a
` generator and which is the `CursorIterable` it is here, given its `Iterable`; and a value
` that is `ByteReadable`, given it as that interface, whose items are what it is `Decodable`
` as, else bytes. An Array is read as an `ArrayTokenStream` of its items, any other
` value that is `Indexable` as an `IndexableTokenStream`, and one that is only `Iterable`
` through a `ChunkedTokenStream`, each given it as that interface.
if subject == invalid-type || subject == no-type
    = false
. kind = types.intrinsic-of(subject)
. given = if kind == .class || kind == .interface then stream-support else no-type
    .. stream-support = supported(subject, types.token-stream-decl)
. ref = class-ref(types, subject)
if given != no-type
    if retyped && conversions.convert(id, id, subject, given, .reason-argument) == invalid-type
        = false
    .. retyped = subject != given
    = record-stream-view
        - id
        - given
        - first-arg(given)
        - encoded || same-decl(ref, types.text-token-stream-decl)
. mark = scratch.types.mark
. item = no-type
. made = types.array-token-stream-decl
. texts = subject == types.string-type
if texts
    item = types.type-row(.char)
    made = types.text-token-stream-decl
    scratch.types.push(subject)
else if same-decl(ref, types.generator-decl)
    item = first-arg(subject)
    made = types.chunked-token-stream-decl
    scratch.types.push(subject)
else if kind == .interface && same-decl(ref, types.cursor-iterable-decl)
    item = first-arg(subject)
    . iterable = class-over(types.iterable-decl, item)
    if item == no-type || conversions.convert(id, id, subject, iterable, .reason-argument) == invalid-type
        = false
    made = types.chunked-token-stream-decl
    scratch.types.push(iterable)
else
    if kind != .class && kind != .struct && kind != .tuple && kind != .interface
        = false
    . readable = supported(subject, types.byte-readable-decl)
    . indexable = if readable == no-type then supported(subject, types.indexable-decl) else no-type
    . iterable = if readable == no-type && indexable == no-type then iterable-support else no-type
        .. iterable-support = supported(subject, types.iterable-decl)
    . read = readable
    if readable != no-type
        . decodable = supported(subject, types.decodable-decl)
        item = if decodable != no-type then first-arg(decodable) else types.type-row(.uint8)
        made = types.chunked-token-stream-decl
    else if indexable != no-type
        item = first-arg(indexable)
        read = if same-decl(ref, types.array-decl) then no-type else indexable
        if read != no-type
            made = types.indexable-token-stream-decl
    else if iterable != no-type
        item = first-arg(iterable)
        read = iterable
        made = types.chunked-token-stream-decl
    else
        = false
    if read == no-type
        scratch.types.push(subject)
    else
        if conversions.convert(id, id, subject, read, .reason-argument) == invalid-type
            scratch.types.rewind(mark)
            = false
        scratch.types.push(read)
if made.module == 0 || item == no-type
    scratch.types.rewind(mark)
    = false
. stream = if texts then types.class-with-args(made.module, made.decl, scratch.types.mark) else class-over(made, item)
. constructs = calls.demand-constructor(stream, mark)
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if constructs == no-instance
    = false
facts.record-call(instance, id, constructs, .call-constructor, scratch.no-fills, false)
= record-stream-view(id, stream, item, texts)

────────────────────
_ do record-stream-view Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - stream TypeId
    - item TypeId
    - encoded Bool

` Records at a stream pattern the calls the reference makes of the stream it runs on, in
` order: its view of its buffer, which is its `pattern-text-view` of the UTF-8 bytes of its
` characters where it is `encoded` and else its `pattern-view`, its `pattern-commit`, and its
` `pattern-extend`, which a stream that may give more input is asked where the pattern reads
` past the end of its buffer.
. view = calls.protocol-getter(stream, view-name(encoded), id)
if !types.is-optional(view)
    = false
. buffer = field-of(types.optional-inner(view), 0)
if encoded && class-arg(types, buffer, 0) != types.type-row(.uint8)
    = false
if calls.protocol-call(stream, program.store-atom("pattern-commit"), id, types.index-type, false, types.index-type).answer == invalid-type
    = false
stream-view = stream-view.buffer = buffer
stream-view = stream-view.type = stream
stream-view = stream-view.item = item
= calls.protocol-call(stream, program.store-atom("pattern-extend"), id).answer == types.bool-type

────────────────────
+ do record-growth Bool
    - stream TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - encoded Bool

` Records at a pattern a function runs on a stream it is given the calls the reference makes of a
` stream that may give more input where the pattern reads past the end of its buffer, in order:
` the stream's view of its buffer, as `view-name` names it for a function that is `encoded`,
` which gives the buffer it then holds, and its `pattern-extend`.
if !types.is-optional(calls.protocol-getter(stream, view-name(encoded), id))
    = false
= calls.protocol-call(stream, program.store-atom("pattern-extend"), id).answer == types.bool-type

────────────────────
_ do stream-arm-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId

` The type of the arms of a stream pattern, joined as the reference joins them, in the order
` written. An arm that raises gives none. An arm with no expression, or one whose body only
` declares lazy locals, gives the text its pattern matched, or what a rule its pattern calls
` gives. One whose pattern is one literal gives that text as it is, which no helper makes. One
` whose body only declares lazy locals and that would ask the helper for a rollback mark has
` no shape here. In a rule that states the `CaptureSpan` of its stream's items, each arm gives
` the span of the items it matched; elsewhere an arm that gives a span a rule gave, which the
` reference reads as text, has no shape here. An arm with no expression that is a sequence of
` parts gives the text it matched whatever its last part gives, made as the type the arms
` give, where its rule has other arms, where that type is text, which leaves the last part's
` value unmade where the arm is alone, where it is optional text and the arm has others or is
` alone in arms that state no type and give their text, though not where the arms give their
` text whatever their last part gives, or where the helper makes that type of
` the stream's items; one that the reference would make of text as a type nothing makes of it
` has no shape here. Where the arms state no type, that type is the one the arm's last part
` gives, which `arms-type` holds the other arms to. An arm that only looks ahead gives the
` text it matched, none, though it joins the other arms as the type of what it looks for, as
` the reference declares it, where the arms state text or no type and those then join as text.
note-observer()
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        . left = stream-arm-type(row.left)
        . right = stream-arm-type(row.right)
        = join-stream-types(id, left, right)
enter-arm(id)
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        if row.pattern == 0 || !tree.lazies-only(row.right)
            = stream-action-type(id, row.pattern, row.right)
        if row.rollback || helping.explicit
            decline(id)
            = invalid-type
    | .node-stream-panic(row)
        check-stream-panic(id, row.pattern)
        = no-type
if spans-source(rule-arming.target)
    = span-arm-type(id)
. sequence = arm-sequence(id)
. alone = sequence && !pattern-arms.joined && rule-arming.target == types.string-type
. kept = valuing
if alone
    valuing = valuing.unvalued = true
. matched = stream-node-type(id)
valuing = kept
if matched == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if sequence && stream-valued(id)
    . wanted = if rule-arming.target == no-type then matched else rule-arming.target
    . optional-text = types.optional-of(types.string-type)
    . spanned = rule-arming.target == no-type && returns-span(instance, rule-arming.capture-root)
    . optional = wanted == optional-text && (pattern-arms.joined || spanned)
    . makes = wanted == types.string-type || optional || helper-made
        .. helper-made = helping.helper != null && source-candidates(wanted).length != 0
    if pattern-arms.joined || makes
        if !makes || !text-items() || observes-span(matched) || !stream-and
            decline(id)
            = invalid-type
        .. stream-and = tree.nodes[id] is .node-stream-and
        . sourced = record-source-text(id, wanted)
        if sourced == invalid-type
            decline(id)
            = invalid-type
        . given = if optional && sourced == types.string-type then optional-text else sourced
        if rule-arming.target == no-type && pattern-arms.joined
            assumed-sources += given
        facts.set-node-type(instance, id, sourced)
        = given
if stream-valued(id)
    if observes-span(matched)
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    plan-valued(id)
else
    . texted = rule-arming.texts && matched == types.optional-of(types.string-type) && arm-spans
        .. arm-spans = returns-span(instance, id)
    . ahead = matched != types.string-type && looks-ahead(id) && text-target
        .. text-target = rule-arming.target == no-type || rule-arming.target == types.string-type
    . whole = joined-target && matched == types.optional-of(types.string-type)
        .. joined-target = sequence && pattern-arms.joined && rule-arming.target != no-type
    . lone = !texted && lone-arm && matched == types.optional-of(types.string-type) && lone-spans
        .. lone-arm = sequence && !pattern-arms.joined && rule-arming.target == no-type
        .. lone-spans = returns-span(instance, id)
    . recorded = if literal-arm(id) then sliced-text(id) else record-source-text(id, wanted-text)
        .. wanted-text = if rule-arming.target != no-type then rule-arming.target else types.string-type
    if untextual || !text-items() || recorded == invalid-type
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    .. untextual = matched != types.string-type && !texted && !ahead && !whole && !lone
    if ahead && rule-arming.target == no-type
        assumed-sources += recorded
        facts.set-node-type(instance, id, recorded)
        = matched
    if lone
        facts.set-node-type(instance, id, recorded)
        = matched
    matched = recorded
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, matched)
= matched

────────────────────
_ do arm-sequence Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether an arm that runs no expression is a sequence of parts, alone or under lazy locals
` it only declares.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-and
        = true
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && arm-sequence(row.pattern)
= false

────────────────────
_ do looks-ahead Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether an arm's pattern only looks ahead, for a part there or not.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        = row.op == .positive-lookahead-op || row.op == .negative-lookahead-op
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && looks-ahead(row.pattern)
= false

────────────────────
_ do literal-arm Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether an arm's pattern is one literal, whose text the reference gives as a constant.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-string
        = true
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && tree.nodes[row.pattern] is .node-stream-string
= false

────────────────────
_ do plan-valued
    - id SyntaxId

` Plans a part of a stream pattern as giving what a rule it calls gives, unless it is a call of
` a pattern given to the rule or a test of an item for a case of a union, whose own plans say as
` much, or a call planned to give its text, which gives what the helper makes of that text where
` the type pass recorded that.
. plan = facts.plan-of(instance, id)
if plan != .plan-pattern-call && plan != .plan-span-call && plan != .plan-case
    facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-stream-value)

────────────────────
_ do holds-count Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a part of a stream pattern counts a part, whose text the reference gives empty over
` items that are no characters.
for node in tree.subtree-start(id) .. < id + 1
    if tree.nodes[node] is .node-stream-length
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do record-stream-text Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Records where a part of a stream pattern gives the text it matched the call that makes it:
` `slice-string` of the part of the stream's buffer it matched. Within a rule typed with no
` helper for the text of a call of it under one, the call is not made, so it is typed outside any
` restriction.
. unmade = helping.span-typing && helping.helper == null
. call = calls.protocol-call
    - stream-view.buffer
    - program.store-atom("slice-string")
    - id
    • restricted !unmade
= call.answer == types.string-type

────────────────────
_ do join-stream-types TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - left TypeId
    - right TypeId

` Two types a pattern may give, as one: where either side gives none, the other's; where
` either is null, the other's as an optional, unless it is one or null; else the two unified,
` or else their union.
if left == invalid-type || right == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if left == no-type
    = right
if right == no-type
    = left
if left == types.null-type || right == types.null-type
    . valued = if left == types.null-type then right else left
    = if nullable then valued else types.optional-of(valued)
        .. nullable = valued == types.null-type || types.is-optional(valued)
. relation = relations.unify(left, right, module)
if relation-legal(relation)
    = relation.unified
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(left)
scratch.types.push(right)
= types.intern-union(mark)

────────────────────
+ do convert-stream-arms
    - id SyntaxId
    - result TypeId

` Converts what each arm of a stream pattern gives to the type of the pattern, where the arm
` is. The type a pattern is declared to give asks for what its arms match as that type, as text
` read as a number or pieces matched as text, and for an integer written with no suffix that it
` holds.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        convert-stream-arms(row.left, result)
        convert-stream-arms(row.right, result)
        =
    | .node-stream-panic
        =
if facts.is-spanning-arm(instance, id)
    =
. given = facts.node-type(instance, id)
=? if given == no-type || given == result
if relations.reads-text-as-number(given, result) && !acts(id)
    . read = relations.compare-explicit(given, result, module)
    if relation-legal(read)
        conversions.record-conversion(id, read, .reason-join, false, no-type, id)
        =
. written = match tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        row.right != 0 && conversions.fitting-literal(arm-value(row.right), result)
    ??
        false
conversions.convert
    - id
    - id
    - given
    - result
    - .reason-join
    - true
    - result == types.string-type || written

────────────────────
_ acts Bool
    - arm SyntaxId

match tree.nodes[arm]
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        row.right != 0
    ??
        false

────────────────────
+ do note-arm-casts
    - id SyntaxId
    - declared TypeId

` Records each arm of a rule's pattern whose action gives a cast to the type the rule states
` (`note-context-cast`). A rule that states none takes its type from its arms, casts and all,
` and one that states `String` has the text of each arm made by a call, as the reference makes it.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        note-arm-casts(row.left, declared)
        note-arm-casts(row.right, declared)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        calls.note-context-cast(action-value(row.right), declared, .cast-return)

────────────────────
_ do action-value SyntaxId
    - action SyntaxId

` What an action gives: its last statement where it is a block.
do match? tree.nodes[action]
    | .node-block(block)
        if block.body.count != 0
            = tree.children[block.body.start + block.body.count - 1]
= action

────────────────────
_ do stream-action-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` An arm that runs an expression where its pattern matched, which gives the arm's value. The
` expression sees as `it` the text its pattern matched, or what a rule its pattern calls gives where
` the pattern is no sequence, as the reference gives it the pattern's value. The text of a sequence
` of items that are no characters is what `slice-string` makes of them. Where the pattern is an
` optional part that gives its text, `it` is that text as an optional, which the part makes where
` its operand passes, a literal's by the slice and any other as `record-source-text` says. Any other
` value a pattern has has no shape here, and `it` in an arm with no pattern, which the reference
` types as the subject but gives empty text, is an error. Nothing reads the value of a pattern whose expression does
` not read `it`. It reads as `location` where its pattern began and ended, or where it is tried
` where it has none. One the reference runs in a function of its own is recorded, and is planned to
` run so where it is not quiet and its own code may panic, which the panic would show; the panic
` pass plans one whose calls may. Nor has an expression that leaves the function, one of a match's
` local rule marked to roll back with no helper, or one that reads a name its pattern may pass
` without capturing. One of a match's own arms marked to roll back where the match has no helper is
` the reference's error, at the match's first arm. One of a rule's marked so with no helper still
` asks for a mark, which the rule's function cannot give where a pattern calls it so. One under a
` helper that cannot roll back makes the match need it to, and one under a helper that can asks it
` for a mark before the expression runs, as does every arm of a rule whose pattern is marked so.
` Under a helper, the names the expression reads, `it` and what it gives are made as
` `materialize-captures` and `materialize-result` say; `it` alone, where a capture materializer
` makes the type the arms give, is made as that type. One that reads a name the helper made as
` another type than it is wanted as, which the reference does, has a shape only where it gives the
` type it gives with the name as it was, as the reference then takes what it gives for that type. A
` name that holds a `CaptureSpan` reads as text, as `observe-spans` says. In a rule that states a
` `CaptureSpan` the arm gives the span of the items it matched, and its expression, whose value the
` reference drops, has a shape only where it gives that type; elsewhere one that gives a span, or
` reads `it` that holds one, which the reference reads as text, has none.
. rolls-back = helping.explicit
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        rolls-back = rolls-back || row.rollback
if rolls-back
    if helping.helper == null && rule-streaming.matched != 0 && within-matched
        frame.diagnose
            - rule-streaming.matched
            - .stated
            - program.store-atom("Pattern @rollback requires a with helper")
        = invalid-type
    .. within-matched = tree.subtree-start(rule-streaming.matched) <= id && id < rule-streaming.matched
    if helping.helper == null && rule-streaming.matched != 0
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    if helping.helper == null
        facts.note-marking-arm(instance, id)
    else
        helping = helping.rolls = true
        note-helper-use(true)
        if helping.helper!.rollback != no-type
            facts.note-marking-arm(instance, id)
            facts.note-asked-mark(first-type-arg(types, helping.helper!.rollback))
            note-mark()
if spans-source(rule-arming.target) && !rule-arming.span
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. forwards-it = forwarding && name-text(forwarded-read(body)) == "it"
    .. forwarding = helping.helper != null && forwarded-read(body) != 0
. it-wanted = types.string-type
if forwards-it && non-text-target && source-candidates(rule-arming.target).length != 0
    it-wanted = rule-arming.target
.. non-text-target = rule-arming.target != no-type && peeled-optional(rule-arming.target) != types.string-type
. it-type = types.string-type
. spans-it = no-type
if pattern != 0
    . reads = mentions(body, "it")
    . slot = arm-slot(id, .slot-it)
    . sequence = tree.nodes[pattern] is .node-stream-and
    if reads && !forwards-it
        spans-it = it-span(pattern, body, slot)
    . saved-unvalued = valuing
    valuing = valuing.unvalued = !reads || (spans-it != no-type && (sequence || calls-stream))
        .. calls-stream = tree.nodes[pattern] is .node-stream-call
    . matched = stream-node-type(pattern)
    valuing = saved-unvalued
    if matched == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
    if spans-it != no-type && !sequence && matched != types.string-type
        spans-it = no-type
    if spans-it != no-type
        it-type = spans-it
        facts.note-spanning-it(instance, id, spans-it)
        frame.assign(slot, spans-it)
    else if !sequence && stream-valued(pattern) && matched != no-type
        plan-valued(pattern)
        it-type = matched
        if slot != no-slot
            frame.assign(slot, matched)
    else
        . held = optional-operand(pattern)
        if reads && held != 0 && text-items() && matched == types.optional-of(types.string-type)
            . made = if tree.nodes[held] is .node-stream-string then sliced-text(pattern) else record-source-text(pattern, types.string-type)
            if made != types.string-type
                decline(id)
                = invalid-type
            plan-valued(pattern)
            facts.set-node-type(instance, pattern, matched)
            it-type = matched
        else if reads
            . made = if text-sourced then record-source-text(id, it-wanted) else invalid-type
                .. text-sourced = sequence || (text-items() && matched == types.string-type)
            if made == invalid-type
                decline(id)
                = invalid-type
            it-type = made
        if slot != no-slot && (text-items() || reads)
            frame.assign(slot, it-type)
else if mentions(body, "it")
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("An arm with no pattern has no \"it\"; read the subject by its name"))
    = invalid-type
if !type-location(id, pattern != 0, body)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. restores [SlotId]
. restored [TypeId]
if helping.helper != null && !materialize-captures(id, body, restores, restored)
    = invalid-type
if !observe-spans(id, body, restores, restored) || it-spanned
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. it-spanned = observes-span(it-type) && spans-it == no-type && mentions(body, "it")
keep-text-spans(body, restores, restored)
. selects = action-selects
. remade [U32]
. unmade [TypeId]
for offset in 0 .. < remade-positions.length
    remade += remade-positions[offset]
    unmade += remade-types[offset]
. was = instances.rows[instance].may-panic
instances.clear-may-panic(instance)
. outer-arm = valuing
valuing = valuing.action-arm = id
. value = check-statement(body)
valuing = outer-arm
if (value == no-type || value == types.void-type) && final-print(body) != 0
    frame.diagnose(final-print(body), .stated, program.store-atom(print-block-text()))
    = invalid-type
. panics-here = instances.rows[instance].may-panic
if was
    instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
if value == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if rule-arming.target == no-type && reads-atom(body)
    pattern-arms = pattern-arms.uninferred = true
if rolled-remakes && (outer || trial-type(body, remade, unmade) != value)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. rolled-remakes = remade.length != 0 && helping.helper!.rollback != no-type
remakes-result = false
if helping.helper != null && value != no-type
    value = materialize-result(id, pattern, body, value, selects, forwards-it)
    if value == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
. raise = if pattern != 0 then final-raise(body) else 0
if raise != 0
    . advice = "call a function that raises it, or write \"?! error\" as the rule's last arm, which raises where no arm before it matches"
    frame.diagnose(raise, .stated, program.store-atom("An arm's action gives the arm's value, so it cannot be a raise; $advice"))
    = invalid-type
if value == no-type || narrowing.exits(body)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. uncovered = uncovered-read(pattern, body)
if uncovered != 0
    if tree.nodes[uncovered] is .node-identifier
        frame.diagnose(uncovered, .stated, program.store-atom(uncovered-text(uncovered)))
    else
        decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. unplain = unplain-slice(body)
if unplain != 0
    frame.diagnose(unplain, .stated, program.store-atom(slice-read-text()))
    = invalid-type
if rule-arming.span
    if value != rule-arming.target || remakes-result || forwards-it
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    facts.note-spanning-arm(instance, id)
else if observes-span(value)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if !remakes-result && outlines(pattern, body, value)
    note-outlined-action(id, body, it-type)
    if !is-quiet(body)
        if panics-here
            facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-outlined-panic)
        panics.note-outlined(instance, id, body)
for position in 0 .. < restores.length
    frame.assign(restores[position], restored[position])
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, value)
= value

────────────────────
_ it-span TypeId
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId

` The `CaptureSpan` an action that reads `it` sees it as, as the reference keeps it where the
` action reads it only for numbers its span gives as its text does and `it` is the text of the
` characters the arm's pattern matched: that of a sequence, or of a part that gives the text it
` matched, which is not optional; none where it is anything else, and in a rule that states a
` span.
|? slot == no-slot || !text-items() || rule-arming.span || optional-operand(pattern) != 0
    no-type
|? !(tree.nodes[pattern] is .node-stream-and) && !returns-span(instance, pattern)
    no-type
??
    if reads-span-numbers(body, slot, span) then span else no-type

.. span = class-over(types.capture-span-decl, buffer-item)

────────────────────
_ do reads-atom Bool
    - body SyntaxId

` Whether an action reads a property of an `Atom`, which the reference finds no type for
` where it infers what an action gives, and so takes the action to give none.
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-get-expression(row)
            . held = facts.node-type(instance, row.object)
            if held != no-type && held != invalid-type && holds-atom
                = true
            .. holds-atom = types.intrinsic-of(peeled-optional(held)) == .atom
= false

────────────────────
_ do observe-spans Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - restores [SlotId]
    - restored [TypeId]

` Plans how an action reads the names that hold a `CaptureSpan`, as the reference makes them
` where the action starts, with a helper or none: one that holds the span of the stream's
` characters reads as their text, made by `slice-string` of the items it spans. One the helper
` made as another type is left as that. One that holds a span of other items, or in an
` optional or a list, has no shape here. Keeps the slots it retypes, and their types before.
` False where an action has no shape.
. seen [SlotId]
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier
            . slot = capture-slot(node)
            . position = if slot != no-slot then capture-position(slot, pattern-arms.arm) else U32.max
            if position != U32.max && seen.find(slot) == null
                seen += slot
                . held = facts.node-type(instance, capture-sites[position])
                if !observes-span(held) || restores.find(slot) != null
                    continue
                if !text-items() || !gives-source-span(held)
                    = false
                if reads-span-numbers(body, slot, held)
                    continue
                . made = calls.protocol-call
                    - field-of(held, 0)
                    - program.store-atom("slice-string")
                    - id
                    - no-type
                    - false
                    - no-type
                    - no-type
                    - false
                if made.answer != types.string-type || made.fact == no-fact
                    = false
                facts.record-material
                    - MaterialFact
                        - instance
                        - id
                        - .material-span-text
                        - slot
                        - types.string-type
                        - no-type
                        - made.fact
                restores += slot
                restored += held
                frame.assign(slot, types.string-type)
= true

────────────────────
_ do keep-text-spans
    - body SyntaxId
    - restores [SlotId]
    - restored [TypeId]

` Keeps as the `CaptureSpan` of the characters it matched each name captured over text that an
` action reads only for numbers its span gives as its text does, as the reference keeps such a
` name, with a helper or none, where nothing made it otherwise: as an optional span, read only
` through `?.`, where the name is captured over an optional part. Keeps the slots it retypes,
` and their types before.
if !text-items()
    =
. span = class-over(types.capture-span-decl, buffer-item)
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier
            . slot = capture-slot(node)
            if slot == no-slot || restores.find(slot) != null
                continue
            . text = plain-text(slot)
            if text == no-type
                continue
            . optional = types.is-optional(text)
            if !reads-span-numbers(body, slot, span, optional)
                continue
            restores += slot
            restored += text
            frame.assign(slot, if optional then types.optional-of(span) else span)

────────────────────
_ do plain-text TypeId
    - slot SlotId

` The text a name holds where it is captured, once or as alternatives of one another, over text
` that no repeat holds and the stream's buffer gives no part of, and it does not accumulate:
` text, or optional text where each place it is captured is an optional part. None where it is
` anything else.
. found = no-type
for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-slots.length
    if capture-slots[position] != slot
        continue
    . site = capture-sites[position]
    . plan = facts.plan-of(instance, site)
    . type = facts.node-type(instance, site)
    . optional = type == types.optional-of(types.string-type) && optional-part
        .. optional-part = optional-operand(capture-patterns[position]) != 0
    if capture-accumulating[position] || capture-repeats[position] != 0 || (type != types.string-type && !optional) || plan == .plan-stream-value || plan == .plan-stream-slice || (found != no-type && found != type)
        = no-type
    found = type
= found

────────────────────
_ do reads-span-numbers Bool
    - body SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId
    - span TypeId
    - optional Bool = false

. names = 0
. reads = 0
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-function-syntax
            = false
        | .node-identifier
            if capture-slot(node) == slot
                names += 1
        | .node-get-expression(row)
            if tree.nodes[row.object] is .node-identifier && capture-slot(row.object) == slot
                if row.is-tracked || row.is-optional != optional || row.is-loop || foreign-number
                    = false
                .. foreign-number = !shares-number(span, row.name)
                reads += 1
        | .node-call-expression(row)
            if !optional
                reads += passed-spans(row, slot, span)
= names == reads

────────────────────
_ do passes-spans-only Bool
    - slot SlotId
    - body SyntaxId

` Whether an action gives a name captured over text to a function that takes its span, and
` reads it otherwise only for numbers its span gives as its text does (`reads-span-numbers`).
. passed = false
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-call-expression(row)
            passed = passed || passed-spans(row, slot, class-over(types.capture-span-decl, buffer-item)) != 0
= passed && reads-span-numbers(body, slot, class-over(types.capture-span-decl, buffer-item))

────────────────────
_ do passed-spans Int
    - call ASTCallExpression
    - slot SlotId
    - span TypeId

` How many times a call gives a name, alone, as a positional argument that no named one precedes,
` to a function that takes its span there (`takes-span`).
. passed = 0
. position = 0u32
for arg in tree.children[call.args]
    . expr = arg
    . optional = false
    do match? tree.nodes[arg]
        | .node-argument(argument)
            if argument.name
                break
            expr = argument.expr
            optional = argument.is-optional
    if !optional && captured-name && takes-span(call, position, span)
        passed += 1
    .. captured-name = tree.nodes[expr] is .node-identifier && capture-slot(expr) == slot
    position += 1
= passed

────────────────────
_ do takes-span Bool
    - call ASTCallExpression
    - position U32
    - span TypeId

` Whether a call by a name alone reaches a function that states a `CaptureSpan` for the parameter
` at a position, as the reference finds one among the functions of a module the name looks up:
` one that is no method, takes no list of the rest, and is seen from here.
if call.is-curried || call.param-count != 0
    = false
. callee Atom? = null
do match? tree.nodes[call.callable]
    | .node-identifier(read)
        callee = read.name
if !callee
    = false
for candidate in program.lookup(module, callee)
    . target = program.modules[candidate.module]
    do match? target.decls[candidate.decl]
        | .decl-function(fn)
            if fn.owner == 0 && fn.kind == .function-decl && positional && visible
                . types-mark = types.scratch.types.mark
                . names-mark = types.scratch.names.mark
                . signature = signature-into
                    - types
                    - candidate.module
                    - candidate.decl
                    - no-type-arguments(types)
                    - no-type
                    - true
                . wanted = in-signature && same-class(types, signature.args[position], span)
                    .. in-signature = position < signature.args.length
                types.scratch.types.rewind(types-mark)
                types.scratch.names.rewind(names-mark)
                if wanted
                    = true
            .. positional = fn.variadic-index == U32.max && position < fn.args.count
            .. visible = fn.access == .public-access || candidate.module == module
= false

────────────────────
_ shares-number Bool
    - span TypeId
    - name Atom

|? class-arg(types, span, 0) != types.type-row(.char) || !found || !text
    false
??
    is-numeric(types, type) && type == member-type(types.properties[text], types.string-type)

.. found = property-named(span, name)
.. text = property-named(types.string-type, name)
.. type = member-type(types.properties[found], span)

────────────────────
_ do observes-span Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether a value holds a `CaptureSpan`, itself or in an optional or a list, which the
` reference has an action read, and give, as the text or the items it spans.
if type == no-type || type == invalid-type
    = false
. inner = peeled-optional(type)
do match? types.rows[inner]
    | .type-class(row)
        if types.capture-span-decl.refers-to(row.module, row.decl)
            = true
        if types.list-decl.refers-to(row.module, row.decl) || immutable-array
            = observes-span(class-arg(types, inner, 0))
        .. immutable-array = types.immutable-array-decl.refers-to(row.module, row.decl)
= false

────────────────────
_ do span-arm-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId

` An arm that runs no expression in a pattern that is to give a `CaptureSpan`: where a rule
` states the span of its stream's items, the arm gives the span of the items it matched, and
` nothing reads what its pattern gives. Any other such pattern has no shape here.
if !rule-arming.span
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. saved-unvalued = valuing
valuing = valuing.unvalued = true
. matched = stream-node-type(id)
valuing = saved-unvalued
if matched == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
facts.note-spanning-arm(instance, id)
= rule-arming.target

────────────────────
+ gives-source-span Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether a type a rule states is the `CaptureSpan` of the items its stream holds, over the
` buffer the stream reads. The reference then has each arm of the rule give the span of the
` items it matched, whatever its pattern or its action gives.
|? type == no-type || type == invalid-type || types.is-optional(type) || !spans-source(type)
    false
??
    stream-view.item != no-type && over-buffer && field-of(type, 0) == stream-view.buffer

.. over-buffer = class-arg(types, type, 0) == buffer-item

────────────────────
_ do spans-source Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether a pattern is to give a `CaptureSpan`, optional or not. The reference then gives the
` span of the items the pattern matched, whatever its actions give, which has a shape only
` for the arms of a rule that `gives-source-span` says.
if type == no-type || type == invalid-type
    = false
do match? types.rows[peeled-optional(type)]
    | .type-class(row)
        = types.capture-span-decl.refers-to(row.module, row.decl)
= false

────────────────────
_ do ranged-capture Bool?
    - id SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId

` Whether a name captured over text in a repeat keeps the ranges of its passes, as the
` reference keeps one an action that reads it makes through a capture materializer, wanted as
` a list of text or, where the action is that name alone, as what the arms give. A name some
` actions make so and others read as text has no shape here; null where a choice is ambiguous
` or the pattern has no shape.
. listed = class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, types.string-type)
. made = false
. plain = false
for node in tree.subtree-start(rule-arming.capture-root) .. < rule-arming.capture-root + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-stream-transform(row)
            if row.right != 0 && !tree.lazies-only(row.right) && reads-slot(row.right, slot)
                . forwarded = forwarded-read(row.right)
                . forwards = forwarded != 0 && capture-slot(forwarded) == slot
                . result = if rule-arming.target != no-type then rule-arming.target else listed
                . desired = if forwards && contains-output(result) then result else listed
                . chosen = select-materializer
                    - helping.helper!.captures
                    - buffer-item
                    - desired-leaf(desired)
                    - true
                    - node
                if chosen == invalid-type
                    = null
                if chosen == no-type
                    plain = true
                else
                    made = true
if made && plain
    decline(id)
    = null
= made

────────────────────
_ do results-assumed Bool
    - mark Size
    - result TypeId
    - pattern SyntaxId

` Whether the arms that a helper made values for, where the arms declare no type, chose as they
` would have with the type they join as, which the reference takes. Where any did not, the
` pattern has no shape here. An action taken to make its value again does so where the arms
` give the type it took.
. agreed = true
for position in mark .. < assumed-results.length
    . assumed = assumed-results[position]
    if !agrees(assumed, result)
        agreed = false
    else if assumed.interface != no-type && assumed.value == result
        if !record-result(assumed.site, assumed.value, assumed.interface)
            agreed = false
-= assumed-results[mark .. < assumed-results.length]
if !agreed
    decline(pattern)
= agreed

────────────────────
_ agrees Bool
    - assumed AssumedResult
    - result TypeId

` Whether an action that took its own type for the type the arms give chose as it would have
` with the type they join as: where the type is the same; else where it materializes with
` both or with neither, a name it forwards wanted as the type it would be wanted as selects no
` materializer, `it` forwarded would be no other text, and where the action materializes, the
` helper makes neither type. Where the helper makes the type it took and not the one the arms
` give, the action's value is not made again, which is as the action chose but for the
` function of its own the reference may then run it in: so only where it surely runs none, an
` action with no pattern, one that gives text, or a name, a number or text written alone.
|? assumed.value == result
    true
|? selected != (assumed.selects || values-select(assumed.value))
    false
|? forwarding && changed && selects(assumed.forwarded, result, assumed.backed, assumed.site) != 0
    false
|? assumed.forwards-it && untexted && source-candidates(result).length != 0
    false
|? !selected || (!contains-output(assumed.value) && !contains-output(result))
    true
??
    !contains-output(result) && (assumed.pattern == 0 || gives-text || trivial-action(assumed.body))

.. selected = assumed.selects || values-select(result)
.. forwarding = assumed.forwarded != no-type && contains-output(result)
.. changed = result != assumed.forwarded
.. untexted = peeled-optional(result) != types.string-type
.. gives-text = assumed.value == types.string-type

────────────────────
_ do forwarded-read SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` The name an action's expression is, where it is one name alone, as the reference finds a
` capture an action forwards. None for any other expression.
. inner = body
do match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-block(block)
        if block.body.count != 1
            = 0
        inner = tree.children[block.body.start]
= if tree.nodes[inner] is .node-identifier then inner else 0

────────────────────
_ do capture-position U32
    - slot SlotId
    - arm SyntaxId

` Where among the names the match captures a slot is kept, or `U32.max` for one it does not:
` the place in `arm` where it has one, as a name of a rule's pattern may hold another type in
` another arm.
if arm != 0
    for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-slots.length
        if capture-slots[position] == slot && after-start && capture-sites[position] <= arm
            = position as U32
        .. after-start = tree.subtree-start(arm) <= capture-sites[position]
for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-slots.length
    if capture-slots[position] == slot
        = position as U32
= U32.max

────────────────────
_ do materialize-captures Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - restores [SlotId]
    - restored [TypeId]

` Plans how the helper makes the names an action reads, in the order the expression first reads
` them, as the reference materializes them where the action starts. Each is wanted as the type
` `capture-wanted` says, or, where one could be made as another type and the expression is not
` typed with the first, as the one choice of the others it is typed with, as the reference
` chooses; two such choices are its error. Each is then made as `materialize-capture` says,
` and the expression is typed with what it holds. Notes in `action-selects` whether any name
` selects a materializer. Keeps the slots it retypes, and their types before.
action-selects = false
remade-positions.clear()
remade-types.clear()
. forwarded = forwarded-read(body)
. seen [SlotId]
. positions [U32]
. sites [SyntaxId]
. candidates [TypeId]
. starts [U32]
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier
            . slot = capture-slot(node)
            . position = if slot != no-slot then capture-position(slot, pattern-arms.arm) else U32.max
            if position != U32.max && seen.find(slot) == null
                seen += slot
                positions += position
                sites += node
                starts += candidates.length as U32
                if !capture-wanted(id, position, node == forwarded, candidates)
                    = false
starts += candidates.length as U32
. chosen = choose-captures(id, body, positions, candidates, starts)
if chosen == null
    = false
for offset in 0 .. < positions.length
    if !materialize-capture(id, body, positions[offset], chosen[offset], restores, restored)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do capture-wanted Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - position U32
    - forwards Bool
    - candidates [TypeId]

` The types a name an action reads may be wanted as, first the one the reference wants it as: what
` it holds, or where the action is that name alone and the arms give a type a materializer makes,
` that type; then each other type the materializers that apply to it make, put in what it holds past
` optionals and lists, where one is selected for it. Under a helper with no materializer, only what
` it holds, as is a name that accumulates what rules gave where no value materializer takes one, and
` a name that holds the text of a rule that states another type, which the reference holds as that
` type. Otherwise a name that accumulates, holds a part of the buffer, or holds what a rule gave
` that is the text it matched has no shape here. False where the pattern has no shape.
. name = capture-sites[position]
. natural = facts.node-type(instance, name)
if helping.helper!.captures.length == 0 && helping.helper!.values.length == 0
    candidates += natural
    = true
. plan = facts.plan-of(instance, name)
. backed = plan != .plan-stream-value
if capture-accumulating[position] && !backed && selects(natural, natural, false, id) == 0
    candidates += natural
    = true
if (capture-accumulating[position] && backed) || plan == .plan-stream-slice
    decline(id)
    = false
if !backed && returns-span(instance, capture-patterns[position])
    decline(id)
    = false
. result = if rule-arming.target != no-type then rule-arming.target else natural
. desired = if forwards && contains-output(result) then result else natural
candidates += desired
if backed && desired-leaf(natural) != types.string-type
    = true
for materializer in if backed then helping.helper!.captures else helping.helper!.values
    . candidate = with-leaf(desired, second-type-arg(materializer))
    if candidate != desired && candidates.find(candidate) == null
        . also = selects(natural, candidate, backed, id)
        if also == 2
            = false
        if also == 1
            candidates += candidate
= true

────────────────────
_ do choose-captures [TypeId]?
    - id SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - positions [U32]
    - candidates [TypeId]
    - starts [U32]

` The types the names an action reads are wanted as, as the reference chooses them: each the
` first it may be wanted as, where none may be wanted as another or the expression is typed
` with those; else of the choices of the others, tried in order, that the expression is typed
` with, the one that makes the most names as a materializer does, or the first where none is.
` Two such choices that make as many are the reference's error at the action, which names the
` first two. An action of a closure has no shape here where a choice must be tried. Null where
` the pattern has no shape.
. firsts [TypeId]
. several = false
for offset in 0 .. < positions.length
    firsts += candidates[starts[offset]]
    if starts[offset + 1] - starts[offset] > 1
        several = true
if !several
    = firsts
if outer
    decline(id)
    = null
if accepts(body, positions, firsts)
    = firsts
. found [TypeId]
. second [TypeId]
. count = 0
. most = 0
. picks [U32]
for _ in positions
    picks += 0
. done = false
while !done
    . moved = false
    . place = positions.length
    while place != 0 && !moved
        place -= 1
        if picks[place] + 1 < starts[place + 1] - starts[place]
            picks[place] += 1
            for later in place + 1 .. < positions.length
                picks[later] = 0
            moved = true
    if !moved
        done = true
    else
        . made = 0
        for pick in picks
            if pick != 0
                made += 1
        if made >= most
            . tried [TypeId]
            for offset in 0 .. < positions.length
                tried += candidates[starts[offset] + picks[offset]]
            if accepts(body, positions, tried)
                if made > most
                    most = made
                    count = 1
                    found = tried
                else
                    count += 1
                    if count == 2
                        second = tried
if count > 1
    . options [String]
    for choice in [found, second]
        . parts [String]
        for offset in 0 .. < positions.length
            parts += "${name-text(capture-sites[positions[offset]])}=${choice-key}"
                .. choice-key = type-key(types, choice[offset])
        options += ", ".join(parts)
    frame.diagnose
        - id
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom
            - "Ambiguous pattern action capture materialization: ${" or ".join(options)}"
    frame.mention(found ++ second)
    = null
= if count == 1 then found else firsts

────────────────────
_ do accepts Bool
    - body SyntaxId
    - positions [U32]
    - wanted [TypeId]

` Whether an action's expression is typed with the names it reads holding the types given, as
` `trial-type` types it.
. value = trial-type(body, positions, wanted)
= value != invalid-type && value != no-type

────────────────────
_ do trial-type TypeId
    - body SyntaxId
    - positions [U32]
    - wanted [TypeId]

` The type an action's expression gives with the names it reads holding the types given, as
` the reference tries it, on trial (`trial-checker`). Invalid where it reports any.
. checker = trial-checker(body)
for offset in 0 .. < positions.length
    checker.frame.assign(capture-slots[positions[offset]], wanted[offset])
. reported = facts.diagnostics.length
. value = checker.check-statement(body)
if facts.diagnostics.length != reported
    value = invalid-type
facts.diagnostics.truncate(reported)
checker.close()
checker.retire()
= value

────────────────────
+ do foresee-transition
    - transition SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - wanted [SlotId]
    - found [TypeId]
    - targets [TypeId]

` A transition typed on trial as the group it is in runs it, without its guard: `each` and `it`
` are an item of its stream (`foreseen-item`), or what an `if | p = s` tests, which its pattern
` matches, and then its targets are typed. Its guard is left out, as the reference leaves it
` out where it infers what a case holds, since it may read the machine.
. reported = facts.diagnostics.length
. trigger = tree.state-trigger(transition)
if trigger != 0
    . subject = tree.trigger-subject(trigger)
    . stream = tree.trigger-stream(trigger)
    . item = if subject != 0 then infer(subject) else if stream != 0 then foreseen-item(stream) else no-type
    if stream != 0 && item != no-type && item != invalid-type
        for head in tree.group-heads(items)
            if tree.group-transitions(items, head).find(transition) != null
                . each = bindings.declared-kind-at(frame.slots, head, .slot-each)
                . it = bindings.declared-kind-at(frame.slots, head, .slot-it)
                if each != no-slot
                    frame.assign(each, item)
                if it != no-slot
                    frame.assign(it, item)
    if tree.trigger-pattern(trigger) != 0
        if item == no-type || item == invalid-type
            =
        type-trigger-pattern(trigger, item)
if facts.diagnostics.length != reported
    =
for slot in wanted
    found += frame.slot-type(slot)
. given = facts.diagnostics.length
for target in tree.children[tree.state-targets(transition)]
    targets += infer(target)
if facts.diagnostics.length != given
    targets.clear()

────────────────────
_ do foreseen-item TypeId
    - written SyntaxId

` The item the stream a trigger is on gives, as `type-group` finds it: what an event of an
` object publishes, the item of the `Broadcastable` the stream is or converts to, or the item of
` a stream that is only iterable. No type where it is none of these.
. found = infer-found(written, Want().adding(.want-event))
. given = found.type
if found.event != U32.max
    . event = found-events[found.event]
    = event.payload
if given == invalid-type || given == no-type || types.broadcastable-decl.module == 0
    = no-type
if interface-of(given, types.broadcastable-decl) == no-type && iterates-as-source(given)
    = loop-item-type(iteration-container(given, written), written)
. stream = supported(given, types.broadcastable-decl)
if stream == no-type
    = no-type
= first-arg(stream)

────────────────────
+ do trial-checker Checker
    - body SyntaxId

` A checker of its own for an instance of this one's declaration that nothing runs, nested
` where this one is, which reserves only the nodes of a part of the body and knows the slots
` this frame knows, and whose facts are dropped, to type that part on trial.
instances.probes += 1
. row = instances.rows[instance]
. signature = instances.signatures[instance]
. mark = scratch.types.mark
for position in 0 .. < signature.param-count
    scratch.types.push(instances.param-type(instance, position))
. params = scratch.types.since(mark)
. args-mark = scratch.types.mark
for position in 0 .. < signature.args.count
    scratch.types.push(instances.argument-type(instance, position))
. args = scratch.types.since(args-mark)
. probe = instances.intern
    - row.module
    - row.decl
    - row.self-type
    - row.effects
    - row.enclosing
    - params
    - args
    - false
    - no-type
    - U32.max
    - false
    - instances.probes
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
. start = tree.subtree-start(body)
. checker = checker-for(session, probe, outer, true, false, SyntaxRange(start, body - start + 1))
checker.prepare()
for offset in 0 .. < frame.slots.count
    . slot = frame.slots.start + offset
    . known = frame.known(slot)
    if known != no-type && known != invalid-type
        checker.frame.assign(slot, known)
= checker

────────────────────
_ do materialize-capture Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - position U32
    - desired TypeId
    - restores [SlotId]
    - restored [TypeId]

` Plans how the helper makes a name an action reads, wanted as a type, as the reference does
` where the action starts. A name captured over text is made by the capture materializer
` selected for the stream's items and the type wanted, where one is, from its cursors; a name
` that holds a value, by the value materializer selected for its type. An optional name is
` made only where it holds a value; a list of text, one by one, from the ranges its passes
` kept. A name the action reads only for its length, an optional one through `?.`, or gives
` only to functions that take its span (`passes-spans-only`), is left as its text. A name no
` materializer is selected for is left as it is, whatever type it is wanted as, but one that
` holds text for another type has no shape here, nor has such a name the action reads only
` for its length or its span. A name that
` holds a value wanted as its own type, for which the reference selects a value materializer
` that makes another, is made as that other all the same, and noted in `remade-positions`.
. helper = helping.helper!
. name = capture-sites[position]
. slot = capture-slots[position]
. natural = facts.node-type(instance, name)
. backed = facts.plan-of(instance, name) != .plan-stream-value
. ranges = facts.first-material(instance, name)
. chosen = selects(natural, desired, backed, id)
if chosen == 2
    = false
. texted = !backed || desired-leaf(natural) == types.string-type
if chosen == 0
    if !texted
        decline(id)
        = false
    = true
action-selects = true
if backed && !texted && (reads-length-only(slot, body) || passes-spans-only(slot, body))
    decline(id)
    = false
if is-listed(natural)
    = materialize-list(id, position, ranges, desired, backed, restores, restored)
. optional = types.is-optional(natural)
. leaf = if optional then types.optional-inner(natural) else natural
. wanted = if types.is-optional(desired) then types.optional-inner(desired) else desired
if backed && texted && (length-only || (!optional && passes-spans-only(slot, body)))
    = true
.. length-only = reads-length-only(slot, body, optional)
. interface = select-materializer
    - if backed then helper.captures else helper.values
    - if backed then buffer-item else leaf
    - wanted
    - backed
    - id
if interface == invalid-type
    = false
. made = second-type-arg(interface)
if !backed && wanted == leaf && made != leaf
    remade-positions += position
    remade-types += natural
. kind = if backed then MaterialKind.material-capture else MaterialKind.material-value
if !record-material(id, kind, slot, if optional then types.optional-of(made) else made, interface, leaf)
    = false
. typed = if optional then types.optional-of(made) else made
restores += slot
restored += natural
frame.assign(slot, typed)
= true

────────────────────
_ do materialize-list Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - position U32
    - ranges U32
    - desired TypeId
    - backed Bool
    - restores [SlotId]
    - restored [TypeId]

` Plans how the helper makes a name captured in a repeat, one pass at a time, in order, into a
` collector of what it makes, whose list the action reads: for text, each range the passes
` kept, by the capture materializer selected for the stream's items and what the list is
` wanted to hold; for values, each value, by the value materializer selected for its type,
` noted in `remade-positions` where it makes another type than the list is wanted to hold.
if backed && (ranges == U32.max || facts.materials[ranges].kind != .material-ranges)
    decline(id)
    = false
. slot = capture-slots[position]
. natural = facts.node-type(instance, capture-sites[position])
. item = first-arg(natural)
if types.is-optional(item)
    decline(id)
    = false
. interface = select-materializer
    - if backed then helping.helper!.captures else helping.helper!.values
    - if backed then buffer-item else item
    - desired-leaf(desired)
    - backed
    - id
if interface == invalid-type
    = false
. made = second-type-arg(interface)
if !backed && desired-leaf(desired) == item && made != item
    remade-positions += position
    remade-types += natural
. listed = class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, made)
. collector = collector-over(made)
. kind = if backed then MaterialKind.material-capture else MaterialKind.material-value
if collector == invalid-type || !record-material(id, kind, slot, listed, interface, item)
    decline(id)
    = false
. growing = calls.protocol-call(collector, program.store-atom("grow"), id, no-type, false, no-type, no-type, false)
if growing.answer != grown-items(collector) || growing.fact == no-fact
    decline(id)
    = false
facts.record-material
    - MaterialFact(instance, id, .material-grow, slot, collector, no-type, growing.fact)
if listed != natural
    restores += slot
    restored += natural
    frame.assign(slot, listed)
= true

────────────────────
_ do materialize-result TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - value TypeId
    - selects Bool
    - forwards-it Bool

` What an action gives under a helper, as the reference materializes it: an action whose names
` select a materializer, or whose arms give a type a value materializer's output converts to
` better than down, materializes, and has the helper roll back where it implements
` `PatternRollback`. Where the arms give a type a materializer makes, what such an action gives is
` made again by the value materializer selected for it, and the action gives what that makes; but
` not where the action is `it` alone, made as that type already. An optional value is made again
` only where it holds one, where the arms give an optional too, and a list item by item, where
` they give a list; an optional the arms give as what it holds, a list they give as none, and a
` list of optionals or of lists have no shape here. Where the arms declare no type, the action's
` own stands for theirs, as `results-assumed` then checks, and the value materializer selected is
` only noted there, to be called once the arms are known to give that type. An action that
` materializes where the arms give such a type `remakes-result`, which the reference runs where
` its arm does, never in a function of its own.
. helper = helping.helper!
. result = rule-arming.target
. assuming = result == no-type
. natural = no-type
. backed = false
if assuming
    result = value
    . forwarded = if forwarded-read(body) != 0 then forwarded-position else U32.max
        .. forwarded-position = capture-position(capture-slot(forwarded-read(body)), pattern-arms.arm)
    natural = if forwarded != U32.max then forwarded-type else no-type
        .. forwarded-type = facts.node-type(instance, capture-sites[forwarded])
    backed = forwarded != U32.max && plain-forward
        .. plain-forward = facts.plan-of(instance, capture-sites[forwarded]) != .plan-stream-value
    assumed-results += AssumedResult
        - value
        - selects
        - forwards-it
        - natural
        - backed
        - id
        - pattern
        - body
        - no-type
. selected = selects || values-select(result)
if !selected
    = value
pattern-arms = pattern-arms.selects = true
remakes-result = contains-output(result)
note-helper-use(helper.rollback != no-type)
if !contains-output(result) || forwards-it
    = value
. requires = result-requires(value, result, id)
if requires == 2
    = invalid-type
if requires == 0
    = value
. listing = is-listed(value)
. optional = types.is-optional(value)
if (listing && !is-listed(result)) || (optional && !types.is-optional(result))
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. leaf = if listing then first-arg(value) else if optional then inner-value else value
    .. inner-value = types.optional-inner(value)
if types.is-optional(leaf) || is-listed(leaf)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. wanted = if listing then first-arg(result) else if optional then inner-result else result
    .. inner-result = types.optional-inner(result)
. interface = select-materializer(helper.values, leaf, wanted, false, id)
if interface == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if interface == no-type
    = value
. made = remade-as(value, interface)
if assuming
    if made != value
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    assumed-results[assumed-results.length - 1] = AssumedResult
        - value
        - selects
        - forwards-it
        - natural
        - backed
        - id
        - pattern
        - body
        - interface
    = made
if !record-result(id, value, interface)
    = invalid-type
= made

────────────────────
_ do remade-as TypeId
    - value TypeId
    - interface TypeId

` The type a value made again by a value materializer has: what the materializer makes, as
` an optional where the value is one, or a list where it is a list.
. made = second-type-arg(interface)
if is-listed(value)
    = class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, made)
= if types.is-optional(value) then types.optional-of(made) else made

────────────────────
_ do record-result Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - value TypeId
    - interface TypeId

` Records the call of the value materializer that makes what an action gives again: of the
` value; of what an optional one holds, which is made only where it holds one and given as
` the optional of what the materializer makes; or of each item of a list, into a collector of
` what the materializer makes, grown by the call recorded after the materializer's, whose
` list the action then gives. False where the pattern has no shape.
. made = second-type-arg(interface)
if !is-listed(value)
    = record-material
        - site
        - .material-result
        - no-slot
        - remade-as(value, interface)
        - interface
        - if types.is-optional(value) then types.optional-inner(value) else value
. collector = collector-over(made)
if collector == invalid-type || !record-material(site, .material-result, no-slot, remade-as(value, interface), interface, first-arg(value))
    decline(site)
    = false
. growing = calls.protocol-call(collector, program.store-atom("grow"), site, no-type, false, no-type, no-type, false)
if growing.answer != grown-items(collector) || growing.fact == no-fact
    decline(site)
    = false
facts.record-material
    - MaterialFact(instance, site, .material-grow, no-slot, collector, no-type, growing.fact)
= true

────────────────────
_ do values-select Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether what a value materializer of the helper makes converts to a type better than down,
` as the reference finds an action that gives that type materializing.
for materializer in helping.helper!.values
    . relation = relations.compare(second-type-arg(materializer), type)
    if relation-legal(relation) && relation.rank < down-cast-rank()
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do result-requires U8
    - value TypeId
    - result TypeId
    - site SyntaxId

` Whether the reference makes what an action gives again as the type the arms give: where it
` is optional and they are not, or a list and they are not, or what it holds past optionals
` and lists is another type than theirs, or has a value materializer selected for it. 0 for
` no, 1 for yes, 2 where the choice is ambiguous, reported at the site.
if types.is-optional(value)
    = if types.is-optional(result) then result-requires(inner-value, inner-result, site) else 1
        .. inner-value = types.optional-inner(value)
        .. inner-result = types.optional-inner(result)
if is-listed(value)
    = if is-listed(result) then result-requires(first-arg(value), first-arg(result), site) else 1
. chosen = select-materializer(helping.helper!.values, value, result, false, site)
if chosen == invalid-type
    = 2
= if chosen != no-type || value != result then 1 else 0

────────────────────
_ do record-source-text TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - result TypeId

` Records where a part of a stream pattern gives the text it matched as a value, the call that
` makes it: under a helper with a capture materializer that makes the type the value is
` wanted as from the stream's items, that materializer's, as the reference's implicit
` materialization; else the slice `record-stream-text` records. The type the text is given
` as, or invalid where the part has no shape.
if helping.helper == null
    = sliced-text(id)
. candidates = source-candidates(result)
if candidates.length == 0
    = sliced-text(id)
. interface = select-materializer(candidates, buffer-item, peeled-optional(result), true, id)
if interface == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if interface == no-type
    = sliced-text(id)
. made = second-type-arg(interface)
= if record-material(id, .material-text, no-slot, made, interface, no-type) then made else invalid-type

────────────────────
_ do sliced-text TypeId
    - id SyntaxId

` The type of the text a part of a stream pattern gives as `record-stream-text` records it.
= if record-stream-text(id) then types.string-type else invalid-type

────────────────────
_ do source-candidates [TypeId]
    - result TypeId

` The capture materializers of the helper that make the type a value is wanted as, what it
` holds where it is optional.
. wanted = peeled-optional(result)
. found [TypeId]
for materializer in helping.helper!.captures
    if second-type-arg(materializer) == wanted
        found += materializer
= found

────────────────────
_ do peeled-optional TypeId
    - type TypeId

. current = type
while types.is-optional(current)
    current = types.optional-inner(current)
= current

────────────────────
_ is-listed Bool
    - type TypeId

same-decl(class-ref(types, type), types.immutable-array-decl)

────────────────────
_ desired-leaf TypeId
    - type TypeId

` What a type a value is wanted as holds, past optionals and lists, as the reference selects a
` materializer for it.
if is-listed(current) then desired-leaf(first-arg(current)) else current

.. current = peeled-optional(type)

────────────────────
_ do with-leaf TypeId
    - type TypeId
    - leaf TypeId

` A type a value is wanted as, with what it holds past optionals and lists another type.
if types.is-optional(type)
    = types.optional-of(with-leaf(types.optional-inner(type), leaf))
if is-listed(type)
    = class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, with-leaf(first-arg(type), leaf))
= leaf

────────────────────
_ do contains-output Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether what a type holds past optionals and lists is what one of the helper's materializers
` makes.
. leaf = desired-leaf(type)
for materializer in helping.helper!.captures
    if second-type-arg(materializer) == leaf
        = true
for materializer in helping.helper!.values
    if second-type-arg(materializer) == leaf
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do selects U8
    - type TypeId
    - desired TypeId
    - backed Bool
    - site SyntaxId

` Whether the helper selects a materializer for a name of a type wanted as another, past
` optionals and lists: for a name captured over text, a capture materializer of the stream's
` items; else a value materializer of what it holds, which for a value wanted as its own type
` must make that type. 0 for none, 1 for one, 2 where the choice is ambiguous, reported at the
` site.
. held = peeled-optional(type)
. wanted = if types.is-optional(desired) then types.optional-inner(desired) else desired
if is-listed(held)
    held = first-arg(held)
    wanted = if is-listed(wanted) then first-arg(wanted) else wanted
. chosen = select-materializer
    - if backed then helping.helper!.captures else helping.helper!.values
    - if backed then buffer-item else held
    - wanted
    - backed
    - site
if chosen == invalid-type
    = 2
if chosen == no-type
    = 0
if !backed && held == wanted
    . made = relations.compare(second-type-arg(chosen), desired-leaf(wanted))
    if !relation-legal(made) || made.rank >= down-cast-rank()
        = 0
= 1

────────────────────
_ do select-materializer TypeId
    - candidates [TypeId]
    - input TypeId
    - desired TypeId
    - capture Bool
    - site SyntaxId

` The materializer the reference selects among some for an input and a type wanted: of those
` that take the input better than down, and a union only as itself, those that take it as it
` is where any does; of those, the ones whose output
` converts to what the wanted type holds better than down, or else all; the one whose
` conversion ranks best, its output's to the wanted type or else to the input's own text. None
` where none takes the input; a tie is the reference's error at the site.
. leaf = if desired != no-type then desired-leaf(desired) else no-type
. fallback = input
if capture
    fallback = if text-items() then types.string-type else class-over(types.array-decl, input)
. compatible [TypeId]
. ranks [I32]
. fits [Bool]
. exact = false
for candidate in candidates
    exact = exact || (first-type-arg(types, candidate) == input && takes-input(candidate, input))
for candidate in candidates
    if !takes-input(candidate, input) || (exact && first-type-arg(types, candidate) != input)
        continue
    . output = second-type-arg(candidate)
    . fit = false
    . rank = I32.max
    if leaf != no-type
        . given = relations.compare(output, leaf)
        if relation-legal(given) && given.rank < down-cast-rank()
            fit = true
            rank = given.rank
    if !fit
        . plain = relations.compare(output, fallback)
        if relation-legal(plain) && plain.rank < down-cast-rank()
            rank = plain.rank
    compatible += candidate
    ranks += rank
    fits += fit
. any-fit = fits.find(true) != null
. best = I32.max
for position in 0 .. < compatible.length
    if (fits[position] || !any-fit) && ranks[position] < best
        best = ranks[position]
. chosen [TypeId]
for position in 0 .. < compatible.length
    if (fits[position] || !any-fit) && ranks[position] == best
        chosen += compatible[position]
if chosen.length > 1
    . keys [String]
    for type in chosen
        keys += type-key(types, type)
    . named = ", ".join(keys)
    . wanted = if desired != no-type then type-key(types, desired) else "*"
    . capability = if capture then "PatternCaptureMaterializer" else "PatternValueMaterializer"
    frame.diagnose(site, .stated, program.store-atom("Pattern helper has ambiguous $capability capabilities for input ${type-key(types, input)}, output $wanted: $named"), input, desired)
    frame.mention(chosen)
    = invalid-type
= if chosen.length != 0 then chosen[0] else no-type

────────────────────
_ takes-input Bool
    - candidate TypeId
    - input TypeId

|? unites(input) && input != accepted
    false
??
    relation-legal(taken) && taken.rank < down-cast-rank()

.. accepted = first-type-arg(types, candidate)
.. taken = relations.compare(input, accepted)

────────────────────
_ do unites Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether a type is a union as the reference holds one: one written of its cases, or one a
` module declares.
do match? types.rows[type]
    | .type-union
        = true
    | .type-named-union
        = true
    | .type-class
        = types.intrinsic-of(type) == .union
= false

────────────────────
_ down-cast-rank RelationRank

relation-rank(.relation-down-cast)

────────────────────
_ second-type-arg TypeId
    - type TypeId

match types.rows[type]
    | .type-class(row)
        if row.args.count > 1 then types.child-type(row.args, 1) else no-type
    ??
        no-type

────────────────────
+ do capability-receiver TypeId
    - participant TypeId
    - interface TypeId

` The type of what answers a capability interface for a helper, a materializer, a collector
` storage or a record boundary: the helper, or what the property it delegates that interface to
` holds, its initializer typed where it declares no type, followed while that delegates it again.
` None where such a property has no type.
. current = participant
. visited [TypeId]
while visited.find(current) == null
    visited += current
    . pairs = types.delegates-of(current)
    . delegated = false
    . next = no-type
    for offset in 0 .. < pairs.length / 2
        if pairs[offset * 2] == interface && !delegated
            delegated = true
            next = calls.ranking.delegate-type(current, offset)
    if !delegated
        = current
    if next == no-type || next == invalid-type
        = no-type
    current = next
= current

────────────────────
_ do record-material Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - kind MaterialKind
    - slot SlotId
    - type TypeId
    - interface TypeId
    - input TypeId

` Records the call of a materializer that makes a value at a place, kept apart from the calls
` of its node: `materialize-capture` of the stream's buffer and two cursors, or
` `materialize-value` of the value, on what answers the interface for the helper, reached
` through the properties the helper delegates it to, which the call keeps.
. receiver = capability-receiver(helping.helper!.participant, interface)
. places [U32]
if receiver == no-type || (receiver != helping.helper!.participant && !calls.ranking.delegate-path(helping.helper!.participant, receiver, places))
    decline(site)
    = false
. made = ProtocolCall()
if kind == .material-text || kind == .material-capture || kind == .material-eager
    made = calls.protocol-call
        - receiver
        - program.store-atom("materialize-capture")
        - site
        - stream-view.buffer
        - false
        - types.index-type
        - types.index-type
        - false
else
    made = calls.protocol-call
        - receiver
        - program.store-atom("materialize-value")
        - site
        - input
        - false
        - no-type
        - no-type
        - false
if made.fact == no-fact || made.answer != second-type-arg(interface)
    decline(site)
    = false
if places.length != 0
    facts.calls[made.fact].through = facts.keep-steps(places, calls.step-getters(places))
facts.record-material
    - MaterialFact(instance, site, kind, slot, type, interface, made.fact)
note-helper-use(false)
= true

────────────────────
_ do note-helper-use
    - rolls Bool

` Notes that the pattern of a rule typed for a helper makes a value through it, or needs it to
` roll back, where the helper is the rule's and not that of a match in one of its actions.
if rule-helper-site == 0 || helping.site != rule-helper-site
    =
instances.rows[instance].uses-helper = true
if rolls
    instances.rows[instance].rolls-helper = true

────────────────────
_ do note-mark

` Notes that the body being typed holds a rollback mark, which its parts ask the helper for or
` are given by the rules they call: the calls of `mark` and `rewind` that body makes on the
` helper are recorded once, at the body. A rule's own pattern that holds one gives it to the
` pattern calling it.
if helping.body == 0 || helping.helper == null || helping.helper.rollback == no-type
    =
if facts.rollback-body-of(instance, helping.body) == U32.max
    . participant = helping.helper!.participant
    . held = first-type-arg(types, helping.helper!.rollback)
    . made = calls.protocol-call
        - participant
        - program.store-atom("mark")
        - helping.body
        - no-type
        - false
        - no-type
        - no-type
        - false
    . mark-call = made.fact
    . rewinding = calls.protocol-call
        - participant
        - program.store-atom("rewind")
        - helping.body
        - held
        - false
        - no-type
        - no-type
        - false
    . rewind-call = rewinding.fact
    if made.answer != held || mark-call == no-fact || rewind-call == no-fact
        decline(helping.body)
        =
    . kept = if is-integer-kind(types.intrinsic-of(held)) then held else types.optional-of(held)
    facts.add-rollback-body(RollbackBody(instance, helping.body, mark-call, rewind-call, held, kept))
if rule-helper-site != 0 && helping.site == rule-helper-site && helping.body == rule-helper-site
    instances.rows[instance].carries-mark = true

────────────────────
_ do note-observer

` Notes that the body being typed runs under a helper that observes the literal words it
` matches: the calls of `record-pattern-literal` and `rewind-pattern-literals` that body makes
` on the helper are recorded once, at the body.
if helping.body == 0 || helping.helper == null || helping.helper.observer == no-type
    =
if facts.observer-body-of(instance, helping.body) != U32.max
    =
. participant = helping.helper!.participant
. recording = calls.protocol-call
    - participant
    - program.store-atom("record-pattern-literal")
    - helping.body
    - types.index-type
    - false
    - types.index-type
    - no-type
    - false
. record = recording.fact
. rewinding = calls.protocol-call
    - participant
    - program.store-atom("rewind-pattern-literals")
    - helping.body
    - types.index-type
    - false
    - no-type
    - no-type
    - false
. rewind = rewinding.fact
if record == no-fact || rewind == no-fact
    decline(helping.body)
    =
facts.add-observer-body(ObserverBody(instance, helping.body, record, rewind))

────────────────────
_ do note-observed
    - pattern SyntaxId

` Notes that a pattern typed under a helper that observes literal words runs under it, as the
` reference runs one that `observes-literals` says does, which needs the helper to roll back.
if unobserved || !observes-literals(tree, facts, instance, pattern)
    =
.. unobserved = helping.helper == null || helping.helper.observer == no-type
helping = helping.rolls = true
note-helper-use(true)

────────────────────
+ do holds-rollback Bool
    - pattern SyntaxId

` Whether a pattern has a part marked to roll back.
for node in tree.subtree-start(pattern) .. < pattern + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-stream-transform(row)
            if row.rollback
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do reads-length-only Bool
    - slot SlotId
    - body SyntaxId
    - optional Bool = false

` Whether an action reads a name only for its `length`, a number the span it captured has too,
` as the reference keeps such a name as the span it captured; an `optional` name, only through
` `?.`.
. receivers [SyntaxId]
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-get-expression(row)
            if length-read && row.is-optional == optional && !row.is-tracked && !row.is-loop
                receivers += row.object
            .. length-read = row.name == types.length-atom!
. found = false
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    if tree.nodes[node] is .node-identifier && capture-slot(node) == slot
        if receivers.find(node) == null
            = false
        found = true
= found

────────────────────
_ do type-location Bool
    - arm SyntaxId
    - spans Bool
    - body SyntaxId

` Types the `location` an arm of a stream pattern declares where its expression reads it: a
` `MatchLocation` where the arm has a pattern, and else a `TokenLocation`. The call that
` answers where in the input a cursor lies, the stream's `pattern-location-at`, is recorded at
` the arm, after any other, as the reference makes it there before the expression runs. Only
` the stream a match makes, and the one a rule a module declares is given, are known here.
. slot = arm-slot(arm, .slot-location)
if slot == no-slot || !reads-slot(body, slot)
    = true
. type = if spans then types.match-location-type else types.token-location-type
if stream-view.type == no-type || type == invalid-type
    = false
if calls.protocol-call(stream-view.type, program.store-atom("pattern-location-at"), arm, types.index-type).answer != types.token-location-type
    = false
frame.assign(slot, type)
= true

────────────────────
_ do reads-slot Bool
    - body SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId

` Whether an expression, or a function written in it, reads a slot.
for node in tree.subtree-start(body) .. < body + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier
            . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, node)
            if resolution.kind == .resolve-slot && resolution.slot == slot
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do is-quiet Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether an expression cannot panic: a local or a constant named, a literal, a case of an
` anonymous union or a tuple made of them, texts joined or compared, a text printed, and
` blocks of them.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-block(row)
        = all-quiet(row.body)
    | .node-do-block(row)
        = is-quiet(row.body)
    | .node-print(row)
        = facts.node-type(instance, row.body) == types.string-type && is-quiet(row.body)
    | .node-binary-expression(row)
        . texts = text-left && facts.node-type(instance, row.rhs) == types.string-type
            .. text-left = facts.node-type(instance, row.lhs) == types.string-type
        . joins = concatenates || row.op == .equals-op || row.op == .not-equals-op
            .. concatenates = row.op == .concat-op || row.op == .concat-string-op
        = texts && joins && is-quiet(row.lhs) && is-quiet(row.rhs)
    | .node-identifier(row)
        if row.name == types.true-atom || row.name == types.false-atom
            = true
        . slot = capture-slot(id)
        = slot != no-slot && bindings.slots[slot].kind != .slot-lazy
    | .node-integer-syntax
        = true
    | .node-float-syntax
        = true
    | .node-string-syntax
        = true
    | .node-anonymous-case(row)
        = all-quiet(row.args)
    | .node-tuple-syntax(row)
        = all-quiet(row.items)
    | .node-argument(row)
        = is-quiet(row.expr)
= false

────────────────────
_ do all-quiet Bool
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId

for arg in tree.children[args]
    if !is-quiet(arg)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do check-stream-panic
    - id SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId

` An arm that raises what it gives where no arm before it passed: a panic, or an error that
` leaves the function. Its value is evaluated as an assertion's exception is, and reads as
` `location` where the pattern failed farthest. One with a pattern of its own, or that gives
` any other value, has no shape here.
. exception SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[pattern]
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        if row.pattern == 0
            exception = row.right
if exception == 0 || mentions(exception, "it")
    decline(id)
    =
if !type-location(pattern, false, exception)
    decline(id)
    =
. saved = frame.surround
frame.surround = frame.surround.effects = exceptional-effects(saved.effects)
. raised = infer(exception)
frame.surround = saved
if raised == invalid-type || raised == no-type
    =
if is-subtype(types, raised, types.panic-type)
    instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
    =
if is-subtype(types, raised, types.error-type)
    note-outgoing(raised, id)
    facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-raise)
    =
decline(id)

────────────────────
_ do stream-node-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId

` The type the reference declares for a part of a stream pattern that runs nothing: the text
` it matched for a literal, a range of characters or any one, and for a repeat or a count of
` a part; for a call of a rule, what the rule gives. Over integer items, a range of characters
` gives the item it matched and a literal, where nothing reads it, none; each tests items
` against code points they hold, and other text is an error, as is any text over items of
` another type. A sequence has the type of its last part
` and a lookahead that of its operand; an optional part is optional, and alternatives join.
` An optional part whose operand gives an optional is one of that optional, as the reference
` types it, only where nothing reads its value. A repeat or a count of a part gives its text only where the reference reckons the part
` gives the text it matched; a repeat of a part that gives a value, neither text nor optional,
` gives an `ImmutableArray` of the values, kept by a `PatternCollector` whose growing call is
` recorded at the repeat, and so does a count of such a part, or of a `.`, over items that are
` no characters. A count of another part that gives its text is text over any items, as the reference
` types it, though over items that are no characters what it gives is empty, so nothing may
` read it there. Alternatives that call rules are valued by their text only where each rule
` gives its text; where each gives a value of one type that is not optional, they give the
` value of the one that passed, and are planned so, as are alternatives that each test an item
` against a value of one type. Nothing reads what the alternatives of a part that gives the
` text it matched give, as the reference replaces it with that text. A repeat or a count whose value nothing
` reads, of a part that gives neither its text nor a value, gives none, as the reference makes
` none, and so do alternatives whose value nothing reads. Another count of a part that gives a
` value, other alternatives that call rules, and any other part have no shape here.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-string(row)
        if text-items()
            = types.string-type
        if valuing.unvalued && is-integer(stream-view.item)
            if some(row.text.codepoints) • where !item-holds(each as U64)
                = report-unheld(id)
            = no-type
        if stream-view.item != no-type && !is-integer(stream-view.item)
            frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Text in a pattern can only match character or integer items"))
            = invalid-type
    | .node-stream-any
        = if text-items() then types.string-type else stream-view.item
    | .node-stream-char-range(row)
        if char-bound(row.first) && char-bound(row.last)
            if text-items()
                = types.string-type
            if is-integer(stream-view.item)
                if !item-holds(bound(row.first)) || !item-holds(bound(row.last))
                    = report-unheld(id)
                = stream-view.item
    | .node-stream-predicate(row)
        = predicate-type(id, row.predicate)
    | .node-stream-equality(row)
        = equality-type(id, row.value)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        . saved = valuing
        valuing = valuing.unvalued = true
        . left = stream-node-type(row.left)
        valuing = saved
        . right = stream-node-type(row.right)
        = if left == invalid-type then invalid-type else right
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        . saved = valuing
        if returns-span(instance, id)
            valuing = valuing.unvalued = true
        . left = stream-node-type(row.left)
        . right = stream-node-type(row.right)
        valuing = saved
        . items = tests-item(id)
        if (items || stream-valued(row.left) || stream-valued(row.right)) && unspanned
            if valuing.unvalued && left != invalid-type && right != invalid-type
                = no-type
            left = valued-alternatives(row.left, left)
            right = valued-alternatives(row.right, right)
            if left != right || left-unfit || !stream-valued(row.left) || !stream-valued(row.right)
                if left != right && typed(left) && typed(right)
                    . shown = "${type-short-name(types, left)} and ${type-short-name(types, right)}"
                    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("Alternatives give $shown; give each a value of one type"))
                else
                    decline(id)
                = invalid-type
            .. left-unfit = left == invalid-type || left == no-type || types.is-optional(left)
            .. typed = :: type => type != invalid-type && type != no-type
            facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-stream-value)
            facts.set-node-type(instance, id, left)
            = left
        .. unspanned = items || !returns-span(instance, id)
        = join-stream-types(id, left, right)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        . operand = stream-node-type(row.operand)
        if operand == invalid-type || operand == no-type
            = operand
        if row.op == .zero-or-one-op
            . optional = types.optional-of(operand)
            if stream-valued(row.operand)
                if types.is-optional(operand)
                    if !valuing.unvalued
                        decline(id)
                        = invalid-type
                    optional = types.optional-around(operand)
                facts.set-node-type(instance, id, optional)
            = optional
        if row.op == .zero-or-more-op || row.op == .one-or-more-op
            if !text-items() && !stream-valued(row.operand)
                if returns-span(instance, row.operand)
                    = class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, stream-view.item)
                decline(id)
                = invalid-type
            if text-items() && returns-span(instance, row.operand)
                = types.string-type
            = repeated-values(id, row.operand, operand)
        if row.op == .positive-lookahead-op || row.op == .negative-lookahead-op
            if guards(row.operand)
                facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-stream-guard)
            = operand
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        . saved = valuing
        valuing = valuing.unvalued = false
        . captured = stream-node-type(row.pattern)
        valuing = saved
        = captured
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        if row.pattern != 0 && tree.lazies-only(row.right)
            = stream-node-type(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-call
        = stream-call-type(id)
    | .node-stream-type(row)
        = type-node-type(id, row.type)
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        if !counts(id, row.min, row.max == 0) || (row.max != 0 && !counts(id, row.max, true))
            = invalid-type
        . counted = stream-node-type(row.operand)
        if counted == invalid-type
            = invalid-type
        if stream-valued(id)
            = repeated-values(id, row.operand, counted)
        if !returns-span(instance, row.operand)
            if valuing.unvalued
                = no-type
            decline(id)
            = invalid-type
        = types.string-type
decline(id)
= invalid-type

────────────────────
_ do class-error-site SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId

` Where the reference reports a range of characters in a pattern over items that are neither
` characters nor integers, which it cannot test: at the first it meets as it emits the arms in
` turn. Where the pattern has more than one arm and one of them may start with anything, the
` reference first tests the item an arm starts with where the arm must start with one of
` certain characters, and reports that test at the arm. None where no range is met; `U32.max`
` where the pattern is shaped so that where the reference meets one first is not known here.
. arms [SyntaxId]
stream-arms(pattern, arms)
. ranged = false
for arm in arms
    ranged = ranged || range-site(arm) != 0
if !ranged
    = 0
. guarded = false
if arms.length > 1
    . open = false
    for arm in arms
        . first = first-items(arm)
        if first == .first-unsure
            = U32.max
        open = open || first == .first-open
        guarded = guarded || first == .first-ranges
    if guarded && !open
        = U32.max
for arm in arms
    if guarded && first-items(arm) == .first-ranges
        = arm
    . site = range-site(arm)
    if site != 0
        = site
= 0

────────────────────
_ do valued-alternatives TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - type TypeId

` What a side of alternatives that give the value of the one that passed gives: alternatives
` nested there that gave none, typed as part of alternatives that give the text they matched,
` typed again now that their value is read.
=? type if type != no-type || !(tree.nodes[id] is .node-stream-or)
= stream-node-type(id)

────────────────────
_ do stream-arms
    - id SyntaxId
    - arms [SyntaxId]

` The arms of a stream pattern, in the order written.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        stream-arms(row.left, arms)
        stream-arms(row.right, arms)
        =
arms += id

────────────────────
_ do first-items FirstItems
    - id SyntaxId

do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = if row.pattern != 0 then first-items(row.pattern) else .first-open
    | .node-stream-panic(row)
        = first-items(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = first-items(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        . left = first-items(row.left)
        = if left == .first-open then first-items(row.right) else left
    | .node-stream-any
        = .first-any
    | .node-stream-char-range
        = .first-ranges
    | .node-stream-predicate
        = .first-open
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        if row.op == .zero-or-one-op || row.op == .zero-or-more-op || lookahead
            = .first-open
        .. lookahead = row.op == .positive-lookahead-op || row.op == .negative-lookahead-op
        if row.op == .one-or-more-op
            = first-items(row.operand)
= .first-unsure

────────────────────
_ do range-site SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

` Where the reference reports the first range of characters it meets in a part of a pattern
` over items that cannot be tested so: at the range, or at a repeat it scans for. None where
` the part has none, and `U32.max` where one lies where the reference meets it otherwise.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = if row.pattern != 0 then range-site(row.pattern) else 0
    | .node-stream-panic(row)
        = range-site(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = range-site(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        . left = range-site(row.left)
        = if left == 0 then range-site(row.right) else left
    | .node-stream-char-range
        = id
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        . inner = range-site(row.operand)
        if inner != 0 && inner == row.operand && repeats
            = id
        .. repeats = row.op == .zero-or-more-op || row.op == .one-or-more-op
        = inner
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        = range-site(row.operand)
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        if range-site(row.left) != 0 || range-site(row.right) != 0
            = U32.max
= 0

────────────────────
_ text-items Bool

` Whether the stream a pattern reads holds characters, whose parts give the text they matched.
stream-view.item == types.type-row(.char)

────────────────────
+ encoded Bool

` Whether the buffer of the stream a pattern reads holds the UTF-8 bytes of the characters the
` stream gives, as a `TextTokenStream`'s text view does, rather than the characters.
stream-view.buffer != no-type && class-arg(types, stream-view.buffer, 0) != stream-view.item

────────────────────
_ do view-name Atom
    - encoded Bool

` The getter of a stream's view of its buffer: `pattern-text-view` where the buffer holds the
` UTF-8 bytes of its characters, and else `pattern-view`.
= program.store-atom(if encoded then "pattern-text-view" else "pattern-view")

────────────────────
_ do pattern-argument-type TypeId
    - arg SyntaxId

` A pattern given to a rule as an argument, `~ p`, which the reference passes as a function
` the rule calls with the stream: one that is a call of a rule a module declares written
` alone passes the function made of that rule, and any other a function made of the pattern
` where it is written. It is typed over the items of the stream the call reads, as a rule's
` arms are, read as the `TokenStream` of those items the function is given, as a
` `PatternFunc` of those items and what it gives, which asks the stream for more input through
` the calls `record-growth` keeps. One that captures a name is an error, as nothing can read
` it; one that runs an action has no shape here, nor one that reads a name or calls a local
` rule but as `plain-argument` says, which keeps the names its function is given. Under a helper it is typed for the
` helper as a pattern of its own, which holds a rollback mark where the helper can roll back,
` and needs the helper to roll back where its parts do.
. known = facts.node-type(instance, arg)
if known != no-type
    = known
. pattern SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[arg]
    | .node-stream-match(row)
        pattern = row.pattern
. reads [SlotId]
. read-types [TypeId]
if pattern == 0 || stream-view.item == no-type
    decline(arg)
    = invalid-type
. capture = first-capture(pattern)
if capture != 0
    frame.diagnose(capture, .stated, program.store-atom("A pattern given as an argument can't capture names"))
    = invalid-type
if !plain-argument(pattern, reads, read-types)
    decline(arg)
    = invalid-type
. given = class-over(types.token-stream-decl, stream-view.item)
if !record-growth(given, arg, encoded())
    decline(arg)
    = invalid-type
. outer = stream-view
. texts = rule-arming
. rolls = helping
stream-view = stream-view.type = given
rule-arming = rule-arming.texts = false
rule-arming = rule-arming.capture-root = pattern
rule-arming = rule-arming.target = no-type
rule-arming = rule-arming.rule = true
rule-arming = rule-arming.span = false
helping = helping.rolls = false
rule-arming = rule-arming.casting = 0
helping = helping.explicit = false
helping = helping.body = arg
do match? tree.nodes[pattern]
    | .node-stream-call(call)
        if call.params.count == 0 && call.args.count == 0 && rule-of(pattern) == 0
            rule-arming = rule-arming.casting = pattern
. joined = stream-arm-type(pattern)
note-observed(pattern)
. rolled = helping.rolls
if helping.helper != null
    note-mark()
stream-view = outer
rule-arming = texts
helping = rolls
if rolled
    helping = helping.rolls = true
    note-helper-use(true)
if joined == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
. result = if joined == no-type then types.string-type else joined
convert-stream-arms(pattern, result)
facts.set-node-type(instance, pattern, result)
. rule = no-instance
do match? tree.nodes[pattern]
    | .node-stream-call(row)
        if row.params.count == 0 && row.args.count == 0
            . fact = facts.first-call(instance, pattern)
            rule = if fact != no-fact then facts.calls[fact].callee else no-instance
if stream-view.buffer == no-type
    decline(arg)
    = invalid-type
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(stream-view.item)
scratch.types.push(result)
. type = types.class-with-args(types.pattern-func-decl.module, types.pattern-func-decl.decl, mark)
. answer = types.optional-of(result)
. helper = if helping.helper != null then helping.helper.participant else no-type
. start U32 = facts.action-slots.length as U32
if rule == no-instance
    for position in 0 .. < reads.length
        facts.action-slots.append(reads[position])
        facts.action-types.append(read-types[position])
. count U32 = (facts.action-slots.length - start) as U32
. local SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[pattern]
    | .node-stream-call(row)
        if rule == no-instance && row.params.count == 0 && row.args.count == 0
            local = rule-of(pattern)
facts.pattern-arguments.append
    - PatternArgument
        - instance
        - arg
        - result
        - answer
        - given
        - stream-view.buffer
        - rule
        - helper
        - RowRange'U32(start, count)
        - local
facts.set-node-type(instance, arg, type)
= type

────────────────────
_ do plain-argument Bool
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - reads [SlotId]
    - read-types [TypeId]
    - quiet Bool = false

` Whether a pattern given to a rule runs no action and reads no name but a global or one
` `reads-given` says the function made of it can be given, so that the function needs no more
` of the function it is written in. It calls a local rule given no values, the ways the
` reference compiles: written alone, a rule that is such a pattern itself and calls no rule,
` which the function then runs where it calls it, as the reference's function of the rule shows
` no frame where nothing it runs may panic, or a rule of a match in a function that is no rule
` that runs actions and captures names but calls no rule, panics in no arm and reads no name
` but a global, one it declares or one the function can be given; or anywhere in it, any rule
` `gives-arguments` says
` the function can run, as in a rule a module declares. The first is given the rule's arguments
` too wherever it can be, as the rule runs in a function of its own where a helper it makes its
` value through may panic. Keeps the names the function is given, each once, with its type.
` A name the binder resolved nothing for is one the parser left where it tried another way to
` read the text, and is no part of the pattern. One that is `quiet` declines nothing.
for node in tree.subtree-start(pattern) .. < pattern + 1
    . plain = true
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier
            . kind = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, node).kind
            plain = kind == .resolve-none || kind == .resolve-global || reads-given(node, reads, read-types)
        | .node-ref-identifier
            plain = false
        | .node-stream-transform(row)
            plain = row.right == 0
        | .node-stream-panic
            plain = false
        | .node-stream-call(row)
            . rule = rule-of(node)
            if rule != 0
                plain = row.params.count == 0 && row.args.count == 0
                if plain
                    . runs = node == pattern && (plain-rule(rule, reads, read-types) || acting-rule(rule, reads, read-types))
                    . given = gives-arguments(reads, read-types)
                    plain = runs || given
    if !plain
        if !quiet
            decline(node)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do plain-rule Bool
    - rule SyntaxId
    - reads [SlotId]
    - read-types [TypeId]

` Whether a local rule a pattern given to a rule calls captures no name, runs no action, calls
` no rule and reads no name but one the function made of the pattern can be given. Keeps
` those names only where it is.
. pattern = local-rule-pattern(rule)
if pattern == 0
    = false
for node in tree.subtree-start(pattern) .. < pattern + 1
    if tree.nodes[node] is .node-stream-call
        = false
. held = reads.length
if captures-none(pattern, true) && plain-argument(pattern, reads, read-types, true)
    = true
while reads.length > held
    reads.pop()
    read-types.pop()
= false

────────────────────
_ do acting-rule Bool
    - rule SyntaxId
    - reads [SlotId]
    - read-types [TypeId]

. row = instances.rows[instance]
. pattern = local-rule-pattern(rule)
if pattern == 0 || rule-match(program, row.module, row.decl) != 0
    = false
. first = tree.subtree-start(rule)
. held = reads.length
for node in tree.subtree-start(pattern) .. < pattern + 1
    . plain = true
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier
            . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, node)
            . own = resolution.kind == .resolve-slot && from-first && within-rule
                .. from-first = bindings.slots[resolution.slot].syntax >= first
                .. within-rule = bindings.slots[resolution.slot].syntax <= rule
            plain = own || resolution.kind == .resolve-none || resolution.kind == .resolve-global || resolution.kind == .resolve-type || module-function(resolution) || reads-given(node, reads, read-types)
        | .node-ref-identifier
            plain = false
        | .node-function-syntax
            plain = false
        | .node-stream-panic
            plain = false
        | .node-stream-call
            plain = false
    if !plain
        while reads.length > held
            reads.pop()
            read-types.pop()
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do module-function Bool
    - resolution Resolution

if resolution.kind != .resolve-function
    = false
do match? program.modules[resolution.module].decls[resolution.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        = fn.owner == 0
= false

────────────────────
_ do reads-given Bool
    - node SyntaxId
    - reads [SlotId]
    - read-types [TypeId]

` Whether a name a pattern given to a rule reads is one the function made of the pattern can
` be given where the pattern is passed: an argument of the function being typed, which
` nothing tracks, narrowed or captured from a function around it. The reference finds no
` local there. Keeps each once, with its type.
. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, node)
if resolution.kind != .resolve-slot || outer
    = false
. slot = resolution.slot
. row = bindings.slots[slot]
if row.kind != .slot-argument || tracked || frame.is-captured(slot)
    = false
.. tracked = (row.flags /and/ SlotFlag.slot-tracked) != 0
. type = frame.known(slot)
if type == no-type || type == invalid-type || frame.slot-type(slot) != type
    = false
if reads.find(slot) == null
    reads += slot
    read-types += type
= true

────────────────────
_ do gives-arguments Bool
    - reads [SlotId]
    - read-types [TypeId]

` Whether the function made of a pattern that calls a local rule can run the rule: in a rule a
` module declares, the function is given the arguments the rule was given, which it gives the
` function of the local rule, or reads where it runs the local rule itself. Keeps each once,
` with its type, and none where it cannot be given them all.
. row = instances.rows[instance]
if outer || rule-match(program, row.module, row.decl) == 0
    = false
for position in 1 .. < instances.signatures[instance].args.count
    . slot = argument-slot(position)
    if slot == no-slot || tracked || frame.is-captured(slot)
        = false
    .. tracked = (bindings.slots[slot].flags /and/ SlotFlag.slot-tracked) != 0
for position in 1 .. < instances.signatures[instance].args.count
    . slot = argument-slot(position)
    if reads.find(slot) == null
        reads += slot
        read-types += instances.argument-type(instance, position)
= true

────────────────────
_ do pattern-result TypeId
    - type TypeId

` What a pattern given to a rule gives, where a value is a `PatternFunc` of the stream's
` items; none otherwise.
do match? types.rows[type]
    | .type-class(row)
        if pattern-func && row.args.count == 2 && class-arg(types, type, 0) == stream-view.item
            = class-arg(types, type, 1)
        .. pattern-func = types.pattern-func-decl.refers-to(row.module, row.decl)
= no-type

────────────────────
+ names-given-pattern Bool
    - slot SlotId

` Whether a name is a pattern a rule a module declares is given, which the reference reads
` only as `$name` and `\name` call it, and reports as no name anywhere else: in an action, as
` an action it cannot compile.
bindings.slots[slot].kind == .slot-argument && rule-match(program, row.module, row.decl) != 0

.. row = instances.rows[instance]

────────────────────
+ do is-pattern-func Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether a type is a `PatternFunc` of any items.
if type == no-type || type == invalid-type
    = false
do match? types.rows[type]
    | .type-class(row)
        = types.pattern-func-decl.refers-to(row.module, row.decl)
= false

────────────────────
_ do plan-pattern-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - called TypeId

` Plans a part of a stream pattern as a call of a pattern given to the rule, which gives what
` the pattern gives, and whose function answers the optional of it. What the function runs is
` not known, so the rule may panic. In a rule typed for a helper that can roll back, the
` function gives the rollback mark it holds, which the rule's pattern then holds.
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, called)
facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-pattern-call)
facts.set-answer-type(instance, id, types.optional-of(called))
instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
if instances.rows[instance].helper != no-type
    note-mark()
= called

────────────────────
_ do equality-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - value SyntaxId

` What `$value` matches as a pattern runs. A pattern given to the rule the part is in, a
` `PatternFunc` of the stream's items, is called as a rule is, and gives what it gives. Text
` over a stream of characters gives the text it matched: the value is evaluated where the
` part is tried, with the names captured before it in reach; its length is read checked, by
` its `validated-length`, and its characters in turn by its `next-iterator`, as the reference
` reads them, or where the buffer is `encoded`, its count of bytes by its `size`, which are
` compared with the buffer's. A value of a type like the items', as the reference compares
` them, is compared
` with one item, and gives the value. A case of a union of the items named by its symbol alone,
` as `.press`, tests one item for the case, by its number, and gives what the case holds, or the
` item where it holds nothing. A value of any other type has no shape here.
. known = facts.node-type(instance, id)
if known != no-type
    = known
. named = symbol-of(value)
if named && types.intrinsic-of(stream-view.item) == .union
    note-case(id, stream-view.item, named)
    if facts.plan-of(instance, id) == .plan-case
        . held = case-payload(stream-view.item, named)
        . given = if held == no-type || held == invalid-type then stream-view.item else held
        facts.set-node-type(instance, id, given)
        = given
. type = infer(value, if tree.nodes[value] is .node-identifier then Want().adding(.want-pattern) else Want())
if type == invalid-type || type == no-type
    = invalid-type
. called = pattern-result(type)
if called != no-type
    = plan-pattern-call(id, called)
if type != types.string-type
    . relation = relations.compare(type, stream-view.item, false, false, null, module)
    if stream-view.item == no-type || !validate-relation(relation, .similar)
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    facts.set-node-type(instance, id, type)
    = type
if !text-items()
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if calls.protocol-getter(types.string-type, program.store-atom("validated-length"), id) != types.size-type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if encoded()
    if calls.protocol-getter(types.string-type, program.store-atom("size"), id) != types.size-type
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
else if calls.protocol-call(types.string-type, program.store-atom("next-iterator"), id, types.size-type).answer == invalid-type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, types.string-type)
= types.string-type

────────────────────
_ do predicate-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - predicate SyntaxId

` A test of one item of a stream, which gives the item where it passes, a character in a stream
` of them: its expression sees the item as `it`, and is tested as a condition.
. known = facts.node-type(instance, id)
if known != no-type
    = known
. slot = arm-slot(id, .slot-it)
if slot != no-slot
    frame.assign(slot, stream-view.item)
. tested = infer(predicate)
if tested == invalid-type || tested == no-type
    = invalid-type
note-truthiness(predicate, predicate, tested)
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, stream-view.item)
= stream-view.item

────────────────────
_ do guards Bool
    - operand SyntaxId

` Whether a lookahead looks at a test that does not read the item, as `&\{ size <= limit }` does:
` a guard, which tests its condition alone and needs no item, so it passes at the end of the
` input where the condition holds, and a record is given without waiting for one more item.
do match? tree.nodes[operand]
    | .node-stream-predicate(row)
        = !mentions(row.predicate, "it")
= false

────────────────────
_ do repeated-values TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - operand SyntaxId
    - item TypeId

` A repeat of a part that gives a value: an `ImmutableArray` of what each pass gave, whose
` collector's growing call is recorded at the repeat, once. A part whose value is text gives
` the text a rule it ends with gave. A repeat whose value is not read, as a part of a sequence
` before its last is not, gives none and keeps no collector, as the reference makes none.
. known = facts.node-type(instance, id)
if known != no-type
    = known
if valuing.unvalued
    = no-type
. valued = if item == types.string-type && text-items() then ends-with-rule(operand) else (stream-valued(operand) || takes-item(operand))
. collector = if valued then collector-over(item) else invalid-type
if collector == invalid-type || calls.protocol-call(collector, program.store-atom("grow"), id).answer != grown-items(collector)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if takes-item(operand)
    facts.set-node-type(instance, operand, item)
. list = class-over(types.immutable-array-decl, item)
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, list)
facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-stream-value)
= list

────────────────────
_ returns-span Bool
    - owner InstanceId
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a part of a stream pattern of an instance gives the text it matched, as
` `spans-in` says.
spans-in(instances.rows[owner].module, instances.rows[owner].binding, owner, id)

────────────────────
_ do spans-in Bool
    - module ModuleId
    - binding BindingId
    - owner InstanceId
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a part of a stream pattern a function of a module writes gives the text it matched,
` as the reference reckons it where it repeats or counts the part: a part that matches items,
` a count, an arm that runs nothing, and a name captured over, a repeat or lookahead of, or a
` sequence or alternatives of such parts. A call of a rule gives its text where the rule's
` pattern does, and a rule met again while it is asked of does. The instance that runs the
` pattern, where there is one, says what a test of a value matches, and a call of a pattern
` given to the rule does not give its text; where none, one does not give its text.
. source = program.modules[module].tree
. key = ((binding as U64) /lshift/ 32) /or/ (id as U64)
for held in spanning
    if held == key
        = true
spanning += key
. spans = false
do match? source.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-transform(arm)
        spans = arm.right == 0 && arm.pattern != 0 && spans-in(module, binding, owner, arm.pattern)
    | .node-stream-capture(capture)
        spans = spans-in(module, binding, owner, capture.pattern)
    | .node-stream-and(pair)
        spans = spans-in(module, binding, owner, pair.left) && spans-in(module, binding, owner, pair.right)
    | .node-stream-or(pair)
        spans = spans-in(module, binding, owner, pair.left) && spans-in(module, binding, owner, pair.right)
    | .node-stream-unary(unary)
        spans = spans-in(module, binding, owner, unary.operand)
    | .node-stream-call
        spans = called-spans(module, binding, owner, id)
    | .node-stream-string
        spans = true
    | .node-stream-char-range
        spans = true
    | .node-stream-any
        spans = true
    | .node-stream-length
        spans = true
    | .node-stream-predicate
        spans = true
    | .node-stream-equality(test)
        spans = owner != no-instance && !calls-given-pattern(owner, binding, id, test.value)
spanning.pop()
= spans

────────────────────
_ calls-given-pattern Bool
    - owner InstanceId
    - binding BindingId
    - id SyntaxId
    - value SyntaxId

` Whether `$value` calls a pattern given to the rule rather than testing a value: as the type
` pass planned it, or, before it typed the part in the instance being typed, where the value
` is a name that holds a `PatternFunc` of the stream's items there.
|? facts.plan-of(owner, id) == .plan-pattern-call
    true
|? owner != instance || binding != frame.binding || !(tree.nodes[value] is .node-identifier)
    false
|? resolution.kind != .resolve-slot
    false
??
    type != no-type && pattern-result(type) != no-type

.. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(binding, value)
.. type = frame.slot-type(resolution.slot)

────────────────────
_ do called-spans Bool
    - module ModuleId
    - binding BindingId
    - owner InstanceId
    - call SyntaxId

` Whether a rule a pattern calls gives the text it matched: a local rule of the function, or
` the rule of the function its call was resolved to, or where the instance has not resolved
` it, the rule a module declares that the name binds. A call given collectors gives it.
. source = program.modules[module].tree
do match? source.nodes[call]
    | .node-stream-call(written)
        if written.collector-mappings.count != 0
            = true
if binding == no-binding
    = false
. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(binding, call)
if resolution.kind == .resolve-slot
    . slot = bindings.slots[resolution.slot]
    if slot.kind == .slot-lazy && slot.group != 0
        do match? source.nodes[slot.group]
            | .node-declare(declaration)
                do match? source.nodes[declaration.right]
                    | .node-stream-match(rule)
                        = spans-in(module, binding, owner, rule.pattern)
    = false
. fact = if owner != no-instance then facts.first-call(owner, call) else no-fact
if fact != no-fact && facts.calls[fact].callee != no-instance
    . callee = facts.calls[fact].callee
    . called = instances.rows[callee]
    . matched = rule-match(program, called.module, called.decl)
    do match? program.modules[called.module].tree.nodes[matched]
        | .node-stream-match(rule)
            = spans-in
                - called.module
                - session.binder.bind(called.module, called.decl)
                - callee
                - rule.pattern
    = false
if resolution.kind != .resolve-function
    = false
. matched = rule-match(program, resolution.module, resolution.decl)
do match? program.modules[resolution.module].tree.nodes[matched]
    | .node-stream-match(rule)
        = spans-in
            - resolution.module
            - session.binder.bind(resolution.module, resolution.decl)
            - no-instance
            - rule.pattern
= false

────────────────────
_ do stream-valued Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a part of a stream pattern gives what a rule it calls gives rather than the text it
` matched, as the reference's parts give their values: a call of a rule, a name captured over
` one, an optional one, a repeat of one that gives no text or that ends with one, and a
` sequence whose last part gives one that is no text, a test of an item, a type named, a call
` of a pattern given to the rule, a test of a value like the items', and a count of a part
` that gives a value, as a repeat of one does over characters; and alternatives
` `stream-node-type` planned to give the value of the one that passed. A call given collectors
` gives the text it matched, as does one that `span-call` says gives it.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-call(row)
        = row.collector-mappings.count == 0 && (!span-call(id) || spans-valued(id))
    | .node-stream-or
        = facts.plan-of(instance, id) == .plan-stream-value
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = stream-valued(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && tree.lazies-only(row.right) && stream-valued(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        if row.op == .zero-or-more-op || row.op == .one-or-more-op
            if !text-items()
                = stream-valued(row.operand)
            = repeat-unspanned && (stream-valued(row.operand) || ends-with-rule(row.operand))
                .. repeat-unspanned = !returns-span(instance, row.operand)
        = row.op == .zero-or-one-op && stream-valued(row.operand)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = stream-valued(row.right) && (stream-node-type(row.right) != types.string-type || !text-items())
    | .node-stream-predicate
        = true
    | .node-stream-type
        = true
    | .node-stream-equality
        = facts.plan-of(instance, id) == .plan-pattern-call || tests-item(id)
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        if !text-items()
            = stream-valued(row.operand) || takes-item(row.operand)
        = counted-unspanned && (stream-valued(row.operand) || ends-with-rule(row.operand))
            .. counted-unspanned = !returns-span(instance, row.operand)
= false

────────────────────
_ takes-item Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a part of a stream pattern is a `.` over items that are not characters, which gives
` the item it matched where a name captures it or a count takes it, as a name captured over a
` test of the item holds it.
!text-items() && tree.nodes[id] is .node-stream-any

────────────────────
_ do sequence-tests-item Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a part of a stream pattern is a sequence whose value is that of a part that tests
` an item against a value, as `tests-item` says.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = ends-testing-item(row.right)
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = sequence-tests-item(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && tree.lazies-only(row.right) && sequence-tests-item(row.pattern)
= false

────────────────────
_ do ends-testing-item Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a part of a stream pattern ends with a part that tests an item against a value.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = ends-testing-item(row.right)
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = ends-testing-item(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && tree.lazies-only(row.right) && ends-testing-item(row.pattern)
= tests-item(id)

────────────────────
_ do tests-item Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a part of a stream pattern tests one item against a value of a type like the
` items' that `equality-type` typed, or for a case of a union, or is alternatives that each do.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-equality
        . type = facts.node-type(instance, id)
        if facts.plan-of(instance, id) == .plan-case
            = true
        = unpatterned && type != no-type && type != invalid-type && type != types.string-type
            .. unpatterned = facts.plan-of(instance, id) != .plan-pattern-call
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        = tests-item(row.left) && tests-item(row.right)
= false

────────────────────
_ do ends-with-rule Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a part of a stream pattern ends with a call of a rule, whose value is what the part
` gives on each pass of a repeat around it: a call, a type named, or a sequence that ends with
` one or with a name captured over one. A call given collectors gives no value of its own,
` nor does one that `span-call` says gives its text.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-call(row)
        = row.collector-mappings.count == 0 && (!span-call(id) || spans-valued(id))
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = ends-with-rule(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-type
        = true
    | .node-stream-equality
        = facts.plan-of(instance, id) == .plan-pattern-call
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && tree.lazies-only(row.right) && ends-with-rule(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = ends-with-rule(row.right)
= false

────────────────────
_ span-call Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a call of a rule under a helper gives the text it matched rather than what the rule
` gives, as the reference calls a rule whose pattern gives its text for the span it matched,
` which the pattern calling it makes through the helper only where it needs it; so does such
` a call in a rule called so. Over items that are not characters, such a call has no shape. A
` call written alone as a pattern given to a rule passes the rule's function, which makes its
` text itself. A call of a local rule whose value its arm gives runs the rule for its value
` where the rule states a type other than text that no capture materializer of the helper
` makes, as the reference compiles such a call for the type the rule states.
(helped && id != rule-arming.casting && returns-span(instance, id) && !rule-valued(id)) || span-planned

.. helped = helping.helper != null || helping.span-typing
.. span-planned = facts.plan-of(instance, id) == .plan-span-call

────────────────────
_ do rule-valued Bool
    - id SyntaxId

if helping.helper == null || helping.span-typing
    = false
. rule = rule-of(id)
if rule == 0
    = false
. stated = local-rule-declared(rule)
if unstated || peeled-optional(stated) == types.string-type || !value-position(id)
    = false
.. unstated = stated == no-type || stated == invalid-type
for candidate in source-candidates(stated)
    if takes-input(candidate, stream-view.item)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ bare-span Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - rule SyntaxId

|? helping.helper != null || helping.span-typing || id == rule-arming.casting || facts.is-recursive-rule(instance, rule)
    false
|? (stated != no-type && stated != types.string-type) || !returns-span(instance, id)
    false
??
    bare-arm(id)

.. stated = local-rule-declared(rule)

────────────────────
_ module-span Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a call of a rule a module declares that gives text, with no helper in force, gives
` the text it matched rather than what the rule makes, as the reference calls such a rule for
` its span where the value it makes is not wanted: one whose value nothing reads, and one
` captured alone in an arm whose action does not read `it`.
|? helping.helper != null || helping.span-typing || id == rule-arming.casting || !returns-span(instance, id)
    false
??
    valuing.unvalued || bare-arm(id)

────────────────────
_ do bare-arm Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a call is the pattern of an arm whose action does not read `it`, or a name captured
` over it alone, or over it as an optional part, in the sequence of such an arm.
. arms [SyntaxId]
stream-arms(rule-arming.capture-root, arms)
for arm in arms
    if tree.subtree-start(arm) <= id && id <= arm
        do match? tree.nodes[arm]
            | .node-stream-transform(row)
                = row.pattern != 0 && !tree.lazies-only(row.right) && it-unread && own-part
                    .. it-unread = !mentions(row.right, "it")
                    .. own-part = row.pattern == id || bare-part(row.pattern, id)
        = false
= false

────────────────────
_ do bare-part Bool
    - node SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

do match? tree.nodes[node]
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = (row.pattern == id || optional-operand(row.pattern) == id) && !row.accumulating
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = bare-part(row.left, id) || bare-part(row.right, id)
= false

────────────────────
_ do stream-call-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId

` A call of a rule: the type of what the rule gives. A local rule given no arguments is typed
` where it is first called. A rule a module declares is called as its function is, and a
` pattern a name holds as `$name` calls it; a local rule given arguments or types is an
` error. A rule given collectors is typed as `mapped-call-type` says, where it can take
` them, and is TypeScript's error where not; under a helper that makes text, one whose text is
` read has no shape here. Under a helper, a local rule the match runs where it is called and a
` rule a module declares have a shape here, and no other; one whose pattern gives its text is
` typed as `span-call-type` says. A local rule a function of its own
` runs has a shape only under its rule's own helper, the one the rule is typed for or given as
` an argument. A local rule whose body is code is typed as `coded-rule-type` says, given
` nothing. With no helper, a call of a
` rule that gives text gives the text it matched where `bare-span` or `module-span` says.
. known = facts.node-type(instance, id)
if known != no-type
    = known
. result = invalid-type
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-call(row)
        . plain = row.params.count == 0 && row.args.count == 0
        . rule = rule-of(id)
        . coded = coded-rule(id)
        if coded != 0
            if !plain || row.collector-mappings.count != 0
                decline(id)
            else
                result = coded-rule-type(id, coded)
        else if helping.helper != null && rule == 0 && holds-value(id)
            if row.collector-mappings.count != 0
                decline(id)
            else
                result = held-pattern-type(id, row.name, plain)
        else if row.collector-mappings.count != 0 && helping.helper != null && !helping.span-typing
            if !plain || (!valuing.unvalued && helping.helper.captures.length != 0)
                decline(id)
            else
                result = mapped-call-type(id, rule, row.name, row.collector-mappings)
        else if span-call(id)
            result = span-call-type(id, rule, row.name, row.params, row.args)
        else if row.collector-mappings.count != 0
            if !plain || (rule == 0 && holds-value(id))
                decline(id)
            else
                result = mapped-call-type(id, rule, row.name, row.collector-mappings)
        else if rule != 0 && !plain
            frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("A local rule takes no arguments or types; declare it at module level to give it some"))
        else if rule != 0
            . recurs = !beside-rule && rules.find(rule) != null
            if !beside-rule && rules.length != 0
                facts.note-rule-call(instance, rules[rules.length - 1], rule)
            result = rule-type(rule)
            if recurs && result != invalid-type && !record-recursion(id, rule, result)
                result = invalid-type
            if helping.helper != null && facts.is-recursive-rule(instance, rule) && !own-helper
                decline(id)
                result = invalid-type
            else if result == types.string-type && rules.find(rule) == null && bare-span(id, rule)
                facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-span-call)
        else if holds-value(id)
            result = held-pattern-type(id, row.name, plain)
        else
            result = module-rule-type(id, row.name, row.params, row.args)
            if result == types.string-type && plain && module-span(id)
                facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-span-call)
if result == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, result)
= result

────────────────────
_ spans-valued Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a call `span-call` says gives its text gives a value of another type, which its arm
` gives, made from that text.
known != no-type && known != invalid-type && known != types.string-type && value-position(id)

.. known = facts.node-type(instance, id)

────────────────────
_ do span-call-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - rule SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - params RowRange'SyntaxId
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId

` A call of a rule under a helper that gives the text it matched, as the reference compiles
` one: the rule is typed with no helper, a local rule as giving its text whatever type it
` states, and the call has the type the rule states. A call of one that states text, or none,
` gives the text, as a part matching characters does. Where the rule states another type, a
` call whose value its arm gives is made that type from its text, by `record-source-text`,
` or for an optional type what it holds, which the call then gives as the optional; any other
` gives none. Within a rule called so, every such call gives its text. A local rule given
` arguments or types, a pattern given as an argument, a rule a module declares that gives
` another type than text, and items that are not characters have no shape here. Under a helper
` that observes literal words, the rule is typed under the helper, which makes nothing for it,
` so a call within it still gives its text.
if !text-items() || (rule != 0 && (params.count != 0 || args.count != 0))
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
for arg in tree.children[args]
    . given = arg
    do match? tree.nodes[arg]
        | .node-argument(argument)
            given = argument.expr
    if tree.nodes[given] is .node-stream-match
        decline(given)
        = invalid-type
. saved-helper = helping
if helping.helper != null && helping.helper.observer != no-type
    helping = helping.helper = spanning-helper(helping.helper)
else
    helping = helping.helper = null
    helping = helping.site = 0
helping = helping.span-typing = true
. called = if rule != 0 then rule-type(rule) else module-rule-type(id, name, params, args)
. carried-rolls = helping.rolls
helping = saved-helper
helping = helping.rolls = carried-rolls
if called == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
if called != types.string-type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
facts.set-plan(instance, id, .plan-span-call)
. stated = if helped-rule then local-rule-declared(rule) else no-type
    .. helped-rule = rule != 0 && helping.helper != null && !helping.span-typing
if stated == invalid-type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if stated == no-type || stated == types.string-type
    = types.string-type
if !value-position(id)
    = stated
. made = record-source-text(id, stated)
if made == invalid-type || made == stated
    = made
if types.is-optional(stated) && types.optional-inner(stated) == made
    = stated
decline(id)
= invalid-type

────────────────────
_ do local-rule-declared TypeId
    - rule SyntaxId

` The type a local rule's declaration states, or none.
do match? tree.nodes[rule]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        do match? tree.nodes[declaration.left]
            | .node-type-capture(row)
                if row.type != 0
                    = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.type, frame.env)
= no-type

────────────────────
_ do value-position Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether the value of a part of the stream pattern being typed is what its arm gives, as the
` reference requires it of the part: the arm's pattern, the last part of a sequence that is,
` and the pattern of an action that reads it as `it`.
. arms [SyntaxId]
stream-arms(rule-arming.capture-root, arms)
for arm in arms
    if tree.subtree-start(arm) <= id && id <= arm
        = value-site(arm, id)
= false

────────────────────
_ do value-site Bool
    - node SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

if node == id
    = true
do match? tree.nodes[node]
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        if row.pattern == 0 || (!tree.lazies-only(row.right) && !mentions(row.right, "it"))
            = false
        = value-site(row.pattern, id)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = tree.subtree-start(row.right) <= id && id <= row.right && value-site(row.right, id)
= false

────────────────────
_ do mapped Bool
    - mappings RowRange'SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - source AST
    - target SyntaxId

` Whether the collectors a call maps are ones the rule it calls and the pattern calling it
` accumulate, as the reference checks them where it compiles the call: no name of the rule's
` is mapped twice and no name of the caller's receives twice, each name of the rule's is one
` its own pattern accumulates, and each of the caller's one the pattern calling it does. Each
` name of the rule's is the caller's where none is written. TypeScript's error where not.
. callees [String]
. callers [String]
. sites [SyntaxId]
for mapping in tree.children[mappings]
    do match? tree.nodes[mapping]
        | .node-stream-collector-mapping(row)
            . callee = if row.callee then row.callee.text else row.caller.text
            if callees.find(callee) != null
                frame.diagnose
                    - mapping
                    - .stated
                    - program.store-atom
                        - "Accumulating capture $callee cannot be mapped more than once"
                = false
            if callers.find(row.caller.text) != null
                frame.diagnose
                    - mapping
                    - .stated
                    - program.store-atom
                        - "Collector ${row.caller.text} cannot receive multiple mapped accumulators"
                = false
            callees += callee
            callers += row.caller.text
            sites += mapping
for position in 0 .. < sites.length
    if !accumulates-in(source, target, callees[position])
        frame.diagnose
            - sites[position]
            - .stated
            - program.store-atom
                - "Pattern ${name.text} has no accumulating capture ${callees[position]}"
        = false
for position in 0 .. < sites.length
    if !accumulates-in(tree, rule-arming.capture-root, callers[position])
        frame.diagnose(sites[position], .stated, program.store-atom("Collector mapping target ${callers[position]} is not an active accumulating capture"))
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do mapped-call-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - rule SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - mappings RowRange'SyntaxId

` A call of a rule given collectors, as the reference compiles one: the rule, a local one or
` one a module declares, is typed as where it is called plainly, and each name of the rule's
` that a collector is given for adds to the list the caller's name keeps, which for a local
` rule must be a list of what the rule's name accumulates; the emitter checks one a module
` declares. The call gives the text it matched, as the reference's call gives no value of its
` own. One over items that are not characters, or given a name of the caller's not yet typed,
` has no shape here.
if !text-items()
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if rule != 0
    . pattern = local-rule-pattern(rule)
    if !mapped(mappings, name, tree, pattern)
        = invalid-type
    if rule-type(rule) == invalid-type
        = invalid-type
    for mapping in tree.children[mappings]
        do match? tree.nodes[mapping]
            | .node-stream-collector-mapping(row)
                . callee = if row.callee then row.callee.text else row.caller.text
                . given = accumulated-type(pattern, callee)
                if given == no-type || given != accumulator-type(row.caller.text)
                    decline(id)
                    = invalid-type
    = types.string-type
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-call(row)
        if module-rule-type(id, row.name, row.params, row.args) == invalid-type
            = invalid-type
. fact = facts.first-call(instance, id)
. callee = if fact != no-fact then facts.calls[fact].callee else no-instance
if callee == no-instance
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. called = instances.rows[callee]
. source = program.modules[called.module].tree
. pattern SyntaxId = 0
do match? source.nodes[rule-match(program, called.module, called.decl)]
    | .node-stream-match(matched)
        pattern = matched.pattern
if pattern == 0
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if !mapped(mappings, name, source, pattern)
    = invalid-type
for mapping in tree.children[mappings]
    do match? tree.nodes[mapping]
        | .node-stream-collector-mapping(row)
            if accumulator-type(row.caller.text) == no-type
                decline(id)
                = invalid-type
= types.string-type

────────────────────
_ do accumulator-type TypeId
    - name String

` The list the pattern being typed keeps for a name it accumulates, where the name was typed.
for position in rule-arming.capture-base .. < capture-sites.length
    if capture-accumulating[position] && name-text(capture-sites[position]) == name
        = facts.node-type(instance, capture-sites[position])
= no-type

────────────────────
_ do accumulated-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - name String

` The list a pattern keeps of what a name it accumulates in a part of its own adds, or none.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        if row.accumulating && name-text(row.name) == name
            = facts.node-type(instance, row.name)
        = accumulated-type(row.pattern, name)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        . left = accumulated-type(row.left, name)
        = if left != no-type then left else accumulated-type(row.right, name)
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        . left = accumulated-type(row.left, name)
        = if left != no-type then left else accumulated-type(row.right, name)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        if row.pattern != 0
            = accumulated-type(row.pattern, name)
    | .node-stream-panic(row)
        = accumulated-type(row.pattern, name)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        = accumulated-type(row.operand, name)
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        = accumulated-type(row.operand, name)
= no-type

────────────────────
_ do accumulates-in Bool
    - source AST
    - id SyntaxId
    - name String

` Whether a pattern accumulates a name in a part of its own, not in a rule it calls.
do match? source.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        . named = identifier-name(source, row.name)
        = accumulates-own || accumulates-in(source, row.pattern, name)
            .. accumulates-own = row.accumulating && named && named.text == name
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = accumulates-in(source, row.left, name) || accumulates-in(source, row.right, name)
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        = accumulates-in(source, row.left, name) || accumulates-in(source, row.right, name)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && accumulates-in(source, row.pattern, name)
    | .node-stream-panic(row)
        = accumulates-in(source, row.pattern, name)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        = accumulates-in(source, row.operand, name)
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        = accumulates-in(source, row.operand, name)
= false

────────────────────
_ do local-rule-pattern SyntaxId
    - rule SyntaxId

` The pattern of a local rule, by its declaration.
do match? tree.nodes[rule]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        do match? tree.nodes[declaration.right]
            | .node-stream-match(row)
                = row.pattern
= 0

────────────────────
+ holds-value Bool
    - call SyntaxId

` Whether a call of a rule names a local, an argument or the item of a loop, rather than a
` local rule or a rule a module declares.
|? resolution.kind != .resolve-slot
    false
??
    kind == .slot-local || kind == .slot-argument || kind == .slot-loop-item

.. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, call)
.. kind = bindings.slots[resolution.slot].kind

────────────────────
_ do held-pattern-type TypeId
    - call SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - plain Bool

` A call of a pattern given to the rule, `\name`, as `$name` calls one. One given arguments
` or types, or that names a value of any other type, has no shape here.
. type = if plain then infer-identifier(call, name, Want().adding(.want-pattern)).type else invalid-type
. called = if type != invalid-type then pattern-result(type) else no-type
if called == no-type
    decline(call)
    = invalid-type
= plan-pattern-call(call, called)

────────────────────
_ do type-node-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - written SyntaxId

` A type named as a part of a stream pattern, as the reference types it: a call of the type's
` constructor that takes the stream, which gives what the constructor gives where it passes;
` for a number, a call of the rule `num` or `dec` given the type that reads one, where a rule
` of that name takes the stream; else a test of one item for the type, which gives the item.
. known = facts.node-type(instance, id)
if known != no-type
    = known
. class = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, written, frame.env)
if class == invalid-type || class == no-type
    if !report-missing-type(written, frame.env)
        decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. made = stream-constructor-type(id, class)
if made == no-type
    . kind = types.intrinsic-of(class)
    . reader = program.store-atom(if intrinsic-is-float(kind) then "dec" else "num")
    if intrinsic-is-numeric(kind) && reads-stream(reader, class)
        . empty = RowRange'SyntaxId()
        made = module-rule-type(id, reader, empty, empty, class)
    else
        made = item-test-type(id, written, class)
if made == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
facts.set-node-type(instance, id, made)
= made

────────────────────
_ do stream-constructor-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - class TypeId

` A call of the constructor of a type that takes the stream, as a `TokenStream` of its items,
` with the type of the items as its type parameter, as the reference dispatches it. It gives
` what the constructor gives where it passes, as the rule the constructor is: no type where
` the type has no such constructor. A constructor that is no rule, or that gives what it
` captured, has no shape here. A pattern whose buffer is `encoded` calls the constructor typed
` again for that buffer, as `encoded-callee` says.
. stream = class-over(types.token-stream-decl, stream-view.item)
. params-start = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(stream-view.item)
. shapes-start = scratch.call-arguments.mark
scratch.call-arguments.push(CallArgument(null, false, false, false, false))
. types-start = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(stream)
. syntax-start = scratch.syntax.mark
scratch.syntax.push(id)
. arguments = arguments-since
    - shapes-start
    - types-start
    - syntax-start
    - scratch.types.span(params-start, 1)
types.complete(class)
calls.ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
calls.ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
. hit = calls.ranking.dispatch-constructor(class, true)
calls.ranking.release()
. made = no-type
if hit
    if stream-view.type != stream && conversions.convert(id, id, stream-view.type, stream, .reason-argument) == invalid-type
        made = invalid-type
    else
        made = calls.construction-on(id, class, arguments, true, 0, false, true)
scratch.syntax.rewind(syntax-start)
scratch.types.rewind(params-start)
scratch.call-arguments.rewind(shapes-start)
if made == no-type || made == invalid-type
    = made
. fact = facts.first-call(instance, id)
. callee = if fact != no-fact then facts.calls[fact].callee else no-instance
if callee == no-instance || !types.is-optional(made) || no-rule
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. no-rule = rule-match(program, instances.rows[callee].module, instances.rows[callee].decl) == 0
. given = types.optional-inner(made)
if same-decl(class-ref(types, given), types.capture-result-decl)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. chosen = if helping.helper != null then helped-callee(id, callee, false) else plain-callee(callee)
if chosen == no-instance
    = invalid-type
facts.calls[fact].callee = chosen
= given

────────────────────
_ do reads-stream Bool
    - name Atom
    - class TypeId

` Whether the function of a name given the stream, with the type of its items and a type as its
` type parameters, is a rule, as the reference looks for the rule that reads a number of that
` type.
. params-start = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(stream-view.item)
scratch.types.push(class)
. shapes-start = scratch.call-arguments.mark
scratch.call-arguments.push(CallArgument(null, false, false, false, false))
. types-start = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(stream-view.type)
. syntax-start = scratch.syntax.mark
scratch.syntax.push(0)
. arguments = arguments-since
    - shapes-start
    - types-start
    - syntax-start
    - scratch.types.span(params-start, 2)
calls.ranking.begin(arguments.shapes, arguments.types)
calls.ranking.explicit-params(arguments.params)
. hit = calls.ranking.dispatch-function(no-type, name)
calls.ranking.release()
scratch.syntax.rewind(syntax-start)
scratch.types.rewind(params-start)
scratch.call-arguments.rewind(shapes-start)
= !!hit && rule-match(program, hit.module, hit.decl) != 0

────────────────────
_ do item-test-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - written SyntaxId
    - class TypeId

` A test of one item for a type, as the reference tests it: the item's type must relate to the
` type, as it is reported where not, and the test passes where the item is of it. It gives the
` item as the type. An item of the type itself is tested here, and one of a class the type
` derives from or of a union that has the type as a case, which is tested as the type named as
` a pattern tests a value, by what `plan-type-pattern` records at the type written. An item that is a number of another type is
` never of it, as the reference compares the two types alone, so the test never passes.
` The reference first tells the stream the pattern stands at the item, as it does before it
` calls a function that reads the type, and finds none.
. relation = relations.compare(stream-view.item, class, false, false, null, module)
if !relation-legal(relation)
    frame.diagnose
        - id
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("Type has no stream constructor for this stream item type")
    = invalid-type
if stream-view.item != class && intrinsic-is-numeric(types.intrinsic-of(stream-view.item))
    if !record-commit(id)
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    = class
if stream-view.item != class
    if !derives(class, stream-view.item) && types.intrinsic-of(stream-view.item) != .union
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
    . planned = facts.conversions.length
    plan-type-pattern(written, stream-view.item, class, .similar)
    if facts.conversions.length == planned
        decline(id)
        = invalid-type
if !record-commit(id)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
= class

────────────────────
_ do derives Bool
    - type TypeId
    - ancestor TypeId

` Whether a class derives from another, however far.
if types.intrinsic-of(type) != .class || types.intrinsic-of(ancestor) != .class
    = false
. base = types.base-of(type)
while base
    if base == ancestor
        = true
    base = types.base-of(base)
= false

────────────────────
_ do module-rule-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - params RowRange'SyntaxId
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId
    - named TypeId = no-type

` A call of a rule a module declares, as the reference matches it: a call of the function of
` that name given the stream as its first argument, as a `TokenStream` of its items, before
` the arguments written, and the type of the stream's items as its first type parameter,
` before the types written. It gives what the rule gives where the rule passes. Where no
` function of the name takes them, the call is reported as the reference reports it, unless
` an argument has no type, as a pattern given as an argument has none here. A type `named`
` stands for the types written. A function that
` is no rule, a rule that belongs to a type, and one that calls itself without stating its
` type have no shape here, but where the call reads no type yet the rule reports that it
` cannot be typed, as the reference does. Under a helper, the rule runs as `helped-callee`
` says, and a function that is no rule has no shape. A rule given a pattern there runs typed
` for the helper, which it gives each pattern it calls: a pattern written as the argument,
` typed for the helper too; any other has no shape. The names of the pattern its arguments
` read are made before the call as `materialize-arguments` says. A rule typed again for the
` helper runs in place of the rule as it is, whose body this call then leaves untyped, as the
` reference compiles only the one the pattern calls. A pattern whose buffer is `encoded` calls the
` rule, or the function that is no rule, typed again for that buffer, as `encoded-callee` says,
` in place of the one as it is.
if slot-named || stream-view.item == no-type || stream-view.type == no-type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. slot-named = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, id).kind == .resolve-slot
. stream = class-over(types.token-stream-decl, stream-view.item)
if retyped && conversions.convert(id, id, stream-view.type, stream, .reason-argument) == invalid-type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
.. retyped = stream-view.type != stream
. restores [SlotId]
. restored [TypeId]
if helping.helper != null && !materialize-arguments(id, args, restores, restored)
    = invalid-type
. params-start = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(stream-view.item)
. param-count = 1
if named != no-type
    scratch.types.push(named)
    param-count += 1
for param in tree.children[params]
    scratch.types.push(types.evaluate-type(module, tree, param, frame.env))
    param-count += 1
. shapes-start = scratch.call-arguments.mark
. types-start = scratch.types.mark
. syntax-start = scratch.syntax.mark
scratch.call-arguments.push(CallArgument(null, false, false, false, false, null))
scratch.types.push(stream)
scratch.syntax.push(id)
. typed = true
. patterned = false
for arg in tree.children[args]
    . given = arg
    . label Atom? = null
    . optional = false
    do match? tree.nodes[arg]
        | .node-argument(argument)
            given = argument.expr
            label = argument.name
            optional = argument.is-optional
    . written = tree.nodes[given] is .node-stream-match
    . type = if written then pattern-argument-type(given) else infer-argument(given, given-symbol)
        .. given-symbol = argument-symbol(given)
    scratch.call-arguments.push(argument-shape(label, optional, given))
    if helping.helper != null && is-pattern-func(type)
        patterned = true
        if !written
            decline(given)
            type = invalid-type
    typed = typed && type != invalid-type
    scratch.types.push(type)
    scratch.syntax.push(arg)
. arguments = arguments-since
    - shapes-start
    - types-start
    - syntax-start
    - scratch.types.span(params-start, param-count)
. diagnosed = facts.diagnostics.length
. holds = helping.helper != null || encoded()
. mark = if holds then instances.hold() else instances.held.mark
deferring = holds
. result = if typed then calls.function-call(id, name, arguments) else invalid-type
deferring = false
. resolved = instances.held.mark
if result == invalid-type && typed
    . known = false
    . ruled = false
    for candidate in program.lookup(module, name)
        known = true
        . owner = program.modules[candidate.module]
        do match? owner.decls[candidate.decl]
            | .decl-function(fn)
                ruled = ruled || (fn.args.count != 0 && owner.arg-pool[fn.args.start].name?.text == "(stream)")
    . missing = "Rule \"${name.text}\" not found"
    . unruled = "\"${name.text}\" is a function, not a rule; call it outside the pattern"
    . unmatched = "No rule \"${name.text}\" matches ${type-short-name(types, stream-view.item)} items with these arguments"
    . message = program.store-atom(if !known then missing else if !ruled then unruled else unmatched)
    facts.restate(diagnosed, instance, id, .function-not-found, .stated, message)
scratch.syntax.rewind(syntax-start)
scratch.types.rewind(params-start)
scratch.call-arguments.rewind(shapes-start)
for position in 0 .. < restores.length
    frame.assign(restores[position], restored[position])
. answer = invalid-type
. dropped = no-instance
. fact = if result != invalid-type && result != no-type then called-fact else no-fact
    .. called-fact = facts.first-call(instance, id)
. callee = if fact != no-fact then facts.calls[fact].callee else no-instance
if result == invalid-type || result == no-type
    answer = invalid-type
else if callee == no-instance
    decline(id)
else if instances.rows[callee].self-type != no-type || (in-progress && undeclared)
    decline(id)
else if rule-match(program, instances.rows[callee].module, instances.rows[callee].decl) == 0
    if helping.helper != null
        decline(id)
    else
        answer = boundary-type(id, callee, result)
        if answer != invalid-type && encoded()
            facts.calls[fact].callee = plain-callee(callee)
            dropped = callee
else if !types.is-optional(result)
    decline(id)
else
    . chosen = if has-helper then helped-callee(id, callee, patterned) else plain-callee(callee)
        .. has-helper = helping.helper != null
    if chosen != no-instance
        facts.calls[fact].callee = chosen
        answer = types.optional-inner(result)
        if chosen != callee
            dropped = callee
.. in-progress = instances.rows[callee].state == .instance-in-progress
.. undeclared = instances.signatures[callee].return-state != .return-declared
if holds
    instances.release(mark, resolved, dropped)
= answer

────────────────────
_ do materialize-arguments Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId
    - restores [SlotId]
    - restored [TypeId]

` Plans how the helper makes the names of the pattern that the arguments of a call of a rule
` read, as the reference makes them before the call where one selects a materializer: each
` wanted as what it holds, in the order the arguments first read them, made as
` `materialize-capture` says. A call that makes one makes its pattern one that makes a value
` through the helper. A pattern written as an argument reads none. A name read only for its
` length has no shape here. Keeps the slots it retypes, and their types before.
. seen [SlotId]
. arm = top-arm(id)
action-selects = false
. planned = true
for arg in tree.children[args]
    . given = arg
    do match? tree.nodes[arg]
        | .node-argument(argument)
            given = argument.expr
    if tree.nodes[given] is .node-stream-match
        continue
    for node in tree.subtree-start(given) .. < given + 1
        do match? tree.nodes[node]
            | .node-identifier
                . slot = capture-slot(node)
                . position = if slot != no-slot then capture-position(slot, arm) else U32.max
                if planned && position != U32.max && seen.find(slot) == null
                    seen += slot
                    if reads-length-only(slot, given)
                        decline(id)
                        planned = false
                    else if !materialize-capture(id, given, position, facts.node-type(instance, capture-sites[position]), restores, restored)
                        planned = false
if action-selects
    pattern-arms = pattern-arms.selects = true
action-selects = false
= planned

────────────────────
_ do helped-callee InstanceId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee InstanceId
    - patterned Bool

` The instance a call of a rule a module declares runs under the helper of the pattern calling
` it, as the reference compiles the call: the rule typed again for the helper where its own
` pattern makes a value through it or needs it to roll back, which the call then gives it, and
` the rule as it is elsewhere where not. The pattern calling such a rule uses the helper too,
` and needs it to roll back where the rule does. A call of the rule from its own pattern,
` typed for the helper, has no shape here. A rule given its own helper as an argument runs
` under that, and where it needs it to roll back, so does the pattern calling it; where that
` is not yet known and the helper in force cannot roll back, the call has no shape here. A
` rule given patterns typed for the helper is always typed for it, and one given its own
` helper has no shape then. A rule that holds a rollback mark gives it to the pattern calling
` it, which then holds one too; one given its own helper that holds one gives it so only
` where the pattern calling it keeps marks of the same type, and has no shape here elsewhere.
` Under a helper that observes literal words, a rule is typed for the helper first, and runs
` under it where its pattern does (`observes-literals`); a rule given its own helper runs under
` that only where not, and a call of the rule from its own pattern runs it under the helper.
. observed = helping.helper!.observer != no-type
if ambient-position(types, instances, callee) != U32.max && !observed
    = ambient-callee(id, callee, patterned)
. row = instances.rows[callee]
. signature = instances.signatures[callee]
. start = signature.args.start - signature.param-count
. mark = scratch.types.mark
for offset in 0 .. < signature.param-count + signature.args.count
    scratch.types.push(instances.signature-types[start + offset])
. params = scratch.types.span(mark, signature.param-count)
. args = scratch.types.span(mark + signature.param-count, signature.args.count)
. none = ImmutableArray'U32'ArenaBacking()
. helped = instances.intern
    - row.module
    - row.decl
    - row.self-type
    - row.effects
    - row.enclosing
    - params
    - args
    - true
    - no-type
    - U32.max
    - false
    - 0
    - helping.helper!.participant
    - none
    - none
    - U32.max
    - ZoneEntry()
    - no-instance
    - 0
    - helping.span-typing
    - encoded()
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
demand-body(helped)
. recursive = observed && instances.rows[helped].state == .instance-in-progress
if instances.rows[helped].state != .instance-done && !recursive
    decline(id)
    = no-instance
if !instances.rows[helped].uses-helper && !patterned && !recursive
    if ambient-position(types, instances, callee) != U32.max
        = ambient-callee(id, callee, patterned)
    = plain-callee(callee)
if instances.rows[helped].rolls-helper
    helping = helping.rolls = true
note-helper-use(instances.rows[helped].rolls-helper)
if instances.rows[helped].carries-mark
    note-mark()
= helped

────────────────────
_ do plain-callee InstanceId
    - callee InstanceId

` The instance of a rule, or of a function given the stream that is no rule, a pattern calls
` under no helper: the one it resolved to, or where the pattern's buffer is `encoded`, the one
` `encoded-callee` gives.
= if encoded() then encoded-callee(callee) else callee

────────────────────
_ do encoded-callee InstanceId
    - callee InstanceId

` The instance of a rule, or of a function given the stream that is no rule, a pattern calls
` whose buffer holds the UTF-8 bytes of a String: the one typed again as `encoded`, whose own
` patterns on the stream read those bytes, under the helper and for the text it is typed for
` already.
. row = instances.rows[callee]
. signature = instances.signatures[callee]
. start = signature.args.start - signature.param-count
. mark = scratch.types.mark
for offset in 0 .. < signature.param-count + signature.args.count
    scratch.types.push(instances.signature-types[start + offset])
. params = scratch.types.span(mark, signature.param-count)
. args = scratch.types.span(mark + signature.param-count, signature.args.count)
. none = ImmutableArray'U32'ArenaBacking()
. made = instances.intern
    - row.module
    - row.decl
    - row.self-type
    - row.effects
    - row.enclosing
    - params
    - args
    - true
    - no-type
    - U32.max
    - false
    - 0
    - row.helper
    - none
    - none
    - U32.max
    - ZoneEntry()
    - no-instance
    - 0
    - row.spans
    - true
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
demand-body(made)
= made

────────────────────
_ do ambient-callee InstanceId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee InstanceId
    - patterned Bool

` The instance a call of a rule given its own helper as an argument runs under that helper, as
` `helped-callee` says, typed again as `plain-callee` says.
if patterned
    decline(id)
    = no-instance
. ruled = plain-callee(callee)
demand-body(ruled)
if instances.rows[ruled].state != .instance-done && helping.helper!.rollback == no-type
    decline(id)
    = no-instance
if instances.rows[ruled].carries-mark
    note-mark()
    . theirs = facts.rollback-body-of
        - ruled
        - rule-match(program, instances.rows[ruled].module, instances.rows[ruled].decl)
    . ours = if helping.body != 0 then facts.rollback-body-of(instance, helping.body) else U32.max
    if theirs == U32.max || ours == U32.max || kept-differs
        decline(id)
        = no-instance
    .. kept-differs = facts.rollback-bodies[theirs].kept != facts.rollback-bodies[ours].kept
if instances.rows[ruled].rolls-helper
    helping = helping.rolls = true
    note-helper-use(true)
= ruled

────────────────────
_ do boundary-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee InstanceId
    - result TypeId

` A call of a function given the stream that is no rule, as the reference calls it: the stream
` is told the pattern stands at the cursor before, and asked for its view after, which says
` where the function left it and how far it read. It gives what the function gives, which
` the call holds where the function answers an optional, and the result of a `CaptureResult`
` where it answers one. A function that raises errors has no shape here, and a rule declared
` over items whose body is not only `~` arms, which is called so, is an error that says so.
if instances.signatures[callee].errors.count != 0
    if declared-rule(callee)
        . named = match tree.nodes[id]
            | .node-stream-call(row)
                row.name.text
            ??
                "This rule"
        . advice = "give it a \"~\" arm before its \"?!\" arm with any \"|?\" condition in its pattern, or raise from a function an action calls"
        frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("\"$named\" raises, and a rule a pattern calls may raise only where its body is \"~\" arms, the last of which may be \"?!\"; $advice"))
    else
        decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if !record-commit(id)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. view = calls.protocol-getter(stream-view.type, view-name(encoded()), id)
if !types.is-optional(view)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. given = if types.is-optional(result) then types.optional-inner(result) else result
= if capturing then class-arg(types, given, 1) else given
    .. capturing = same-decl(class-ref(types, given), types.capture-result-decl)

────────────────────
_ do declared-rule Bool
    - callee InstanceId

` Whether a function is declared as a rule, over the items of a stream.
. owner = program.modules[instances.rows[callee].module]
do match? owner.decls[instances.rows[callee].decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        do match? owner.tree.nodes[fn.syntax]
            | .node-function-syntax(syntax)
                = syntax.pattern != 0
= false

────────────────────
_ do record-commit Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Records at a part of a stream pattern the stream's `pattern-commit` of the cursor where the
` part begins, which the reference makes there before it calls a function that is no rule.
= calls.protocol-call(stream-view.type, program.store-atom("pattern-commit"), id, types.index-type, false, types.index-type).answer != invalid-type

────────────────────
+ do rule-of SyntaxId
    - call SyntaxId

` The declaration of the local rule a call of a rule names, or none where it names another.
. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, call)
if resolution.kind != .resolve-slot
    = 0
. row = bindings.slots[resolution.slot]
if row.kind != .slot-lazy || row.group == 0
    = 0
do match? tree.nodes[row.group]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        if tree.nodes[declaration.right] is .node-stream-match
            = row.group
= 0

────────────────────
_ do record-recursion Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - rule SyntaxId
    - result TypeId

` Records what the reference does at a call of a local rule beside a match made from the
` rule's own arms. It calls a function it makes of the rule as it calls a function given the
` stream: the stream is told the pattern stands at the cursor before, and asked for its view
` after. That function runs the rule on the stream's view and commits where it ended, by the
` calls a match on the stream records, which are kept at the rule's pattern; the stream, its
` buffer, and the optional `CaptureResult` the function answers are kept with the rule. A
` rule another rule calls back, one called under a helper, and one called on another stream
` than it was first, have no shape here.
. matched SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[rule]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        matched = declaration.right
. pattern = local-rule-pattern(rule)
if pattern == 0 || rules.length == 0 || rules[rules.length - 1] != rule || helping.helper != null
    if pattern != 0 && rules.find(rule) != null && helping.helper == null
        . text = "The local rules of a match cannot call one another in a cycle; declare them below a rule the module declares, whose local rules can"
        frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(text))
    else
        decline(id)
    = false
. place = facts.note-local-rule(instance, rule)
if facts.local-rules[place].stream == no-type
    . stream = stream-view.type
    . item = stream-view.item
    if !record-stream-view(matched, stream, item, encoded())
        decline(id)
        = false
    . mark = scratch.types.mark
    scratch.types.push(buffer-item)
    scratch.types.push(result)
    . captured = types.class-with-args
        - types.capture-result-decl.module
        - types.capture-result-decl.decl
        - mark
    types.complete(captured)
    . adapted = types.optional-of(captured)
    types.complete(adapted)
    facts.local-rules[place].adapted = adapted
    facts.local-rules[place].stream = stream
    facts.local-rules[place].buffer = stream-view.buffer
else if facts.local-rules[place].stream != stream-view.type
    decline(id)
    = false
if !record-commit(id) || !types.is-optional(calls.protocol-getter(stream-view.type, view-name(encoded()), id))
    decline(id)
    = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do coded-rule SyntaxId
    - call SyntaxId

` The declaration of the local rule a call of a rule names whose body is code that runs
` patterns rather than a pattern, or none where it names another.
. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, call)
if resolution.kind != .resolve-slot
    = 0
. row = bindings.slots[resolution.slot]
if row.kind != .slot-lazy || row.group == 0
    = 0
do match? tree.nodes[row.group]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        if declaration.is-pattern && declaration.right != 0 && !stream-match
            = row.group
        .. stream-match = tree.nodes[declaration.right] is .node-stream-match
= 0

────────────────────
_ do coded-rule-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - rule SyntaxId

` A call of a local rule whose body is code, as the reference calls the function it makes of
` it: the stream is told the pattern stands at the cursor before, the code runs, each pattern
` in it on the stream from where the stream stands, and the stream is asked for its view
` after, which says where the code left it and how far it read. The reference's function
` holds the names the code reads; here the code runs where the rule is called, where they
` are. The code is typed where the rule is first called, for the stream it is called on, and
` must give an optional `CaptureResult` of the stream's items, as a pattern in it does, whose
` result the call gives; code that gives anything else, or that calls the rule, is reported
` as the reference reports it. A rule that states a type or is marked to roll back, and one
` called on another stream or under a helper, have no shape here.
. left SyntaxId = 0
. code SyntaxId = 0
. marked = false
do match? tree.nodes[rule]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        left = declaration.left
        code = declaration.right
        marked = declaration.rollback
. stated = false
do match? tree.nodes[left]
    | .node-type-capture(row)
        stated = row.type != 0
if code == 0 || marked || stated || helping.helper != null
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. untyped = program.store-atom("Unable to infer pattern result type")
if coded-rules.find(rule) != null
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, untyped)
    = invalid-type
if !record-commit(id)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. typed = coded-typed.find(rule)
if typed != null && coded-streams[typed] != stream-view.type
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. given = facts.node-type(instance, code)
if typed == null
    . saved-stream = rule-streaming
    . saved-expected = arms-expected
    . saved-unvalued = valuing
    . saved-explicit = helping
    . ran = stream-view
    coded-rules += rule
    rule-streaming = rule-streaming.matched = 0
    rule-streaming = rule-streaming.stream = ran.type
    rule-streaming = rule-streaming.encoded = encoded()
    arms-expected = no-type
    valuing = valuing.unvalued = false
    helping = helping.explicit = false
    given = infer(code)
    . carried-rolls = helping.rolls
    helping = saved-explicit
    helping = helping.rolls = carried-rolls
    valuing = saved-unvalued
    arms-expected = saved-expected
    rule-streaming = saved-stream
    stream-view = ran
    coded-rules.pop()
    coded-typed += rule
    coded-streams += ran.type
if given == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
. view = calls.protocol-getter(stream-view.type, view-name(encoded()), id)
if !types.is-optional(view)
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. held = if given != no-type && types.is-optional(given) then inner-given else no-type
    .. inner-given = types.optional-inner(given)
if held == no-type || !same-decl(class-ref(types, held), types.capture-result-decl)
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, untyped)
    = invalid-type
if class-arg(types, held, 0) != buffer-item
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
= class-arg(types, held, 1)

────────────────────
+ do left-call SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId
    - target SyntaxId
    - seen [SyntaxId]

` The call by which a part of a stream pattern calls a rule before it reads an item, or none:
` the local rule `target`, or for none the rule the module declares that is being checked,
` called directly or through the local rules called first. A call of any other rule is taken
` to read before it calls anything. Such a rule would call itself forever.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-call
        if calls-target(id, target)
            = id
        . rule = rule-of(id)
        if rule == 0 || seen.find(rule) != null
            = 0
        seen += rule
        = left-call(rule-pattern(rule), target, seen)
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        . leading = left-call(row.left, target, seen)
        if leading != 0 || !may-read-none(row.left, List'SyntaxId())
            = leading
        = left-call(row.right, target, seen)
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        . leading = left-call(row.left, target, seen)
        = if leading != 0 then leading else left-call(row.right, target, seen)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        = left-call(row.operand, target, seen)
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        = left-call(row.operand, target, seen)
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = left-call(row.pattern, target, seen)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        if row.pattern != 0
            = left-call(row.pattern, target, seen)
    | .node-stream-panic(row)
        if row.pattern != 0
            = left-call(row.pattern, target, seen)
= 0

────────────────────
_ do calls-target Bool
    - call SyntaxId
    - target SyntaxId

` Whether a call of a rule names the local rule `target`, or for none the rule the module
` declares that is being checked.
if target != 0
    = rule-of(call) == target
. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, call)
= resolution.kind == .resolve-function && resolution.decl == frame.decl && resolution.module == module

────────────────────
_ do may-read-none Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - seen [SyntaxId]

` Whether a part of a stream pattern may match without reading an item, as far as it is
` known here: a call of a rule other than a local one is taken to read.
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-string(row)
        = row.text.length == 0
    | .node-stream-and(row)
        = may-read-none(row.left, seen) && may-read-none(row.right, seen)
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        = may-read-none(row.left, seen) || may-read-none(row.right, seen)
    | .node-stream-unary(row)
        = row.op != .one-or-more-op || may-read-none(row.operand, seen)
    | .node-stream-length(row)
        do match? tree.nodes[row.min]
            | .node-integer-syntax(bound)
                if parse-integer-literal(bound.value).value == 0
                    = true
        = may-read-none(row.operand, seen)
    | .node-stream-capture(row)
        = may-read-none(row.pattern, seen)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && may-read-none(row.pattern, seen)
    | .node-stream-panic(row)
        = row.pattern != 0 && may-read-none(row.pattern, seen)
    | .node-stream-call
        . rule = rule-of(id)
        if rule == 0 || seen.find(rule) != null
            = false
        seen += rule
        = may-read-none(rule-pattern(rule), seen)
= false

────────────────────
_ do rule-pattern SyntaxId
    - rule SyntaxId

` The pattern of a local rule's declaration.
do match? tree.nodes[rule]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        do match? tree.nodes[declaration.right]
            | .node-stream-match(row)
                = row.pattern
= 0

────────────────────
+ do report-left-recursion
    - call SyntaxId

` Reports a call by which a rule calls itself before it reads anything.
. name = ""
do match? tree.nodes[call]
    | .node-stream-call(row)
        name = row.name.text
. text = "\"$name\" calls itself before reading any input, so it never ends; read input before this call, or write the repetition with \"*\""
frame.diagnose(call, .stated, program.store-atom(text))

────────────────────
_ do rule-type TypeId
    - rule SyntaxId

` What a local rule gives, typed where it is first called: its arms are typed as a pattern of
` their own whose names are its own, which reads the stream from where it is called, and
` joined, then converted to the type its declaration states. The reference runs the rule in
` the function that calls it, where the rule reads that function's locals and the names its
` match captured. A rule that calls itself, directly or through other local rules, gives at
` those calls the type its declaration states, and each rule on the way is one the reference
` runs as a function of its own, which answers the optional of what the rule gives; one that
` states no type is an error at the rule. Nor has a rule called under another helper than it was
` typed under, whose values that helper made. One typed for a call that gives its text states
` that it gives text. A rule beside a rule's pattern that is marked to roll back, or whose
` pattern has an arm that is, asks the helper for a mark before each of its actions, as the
` reference does a rule it compiles on its own. One beside a match's pattern that is marked
` so gives the mark to each of its arms. Its arms give their values whether or not the call it
` is first typed at reads what it gives: a later call may.
. left SyntaxId = 0
. matched SyntaxId = 0
. marked = false
do match? tree.nodes[rule]
    | .node-declare(declaration)
        left = declaration.left
        matched = declaration.right
        marked = declaration.rollback
. pattern SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[matched]
    | .node-stream-match(row)
        pattern = row.pattern
if pattern == 0
    decline(rule)
    = invalid-type
. known = facts.node-type(instance, matched)
if known != no-type
    . typed = typed-rules.find(rule)
    if typed != null && typed-helpers[typed] != helping.site
        decline(rule)
        = invalid-type
    = known
. declared = no-type
do match? tree.nodes[left]
    | .node-type-capture(row)
        if row.type != 0
            declared = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.type, frame.env)
if declared == invalid-type
    decline(rule)
    = invalid-type
if helping.span-typing
    declared = types.string-type
. calling = rules.find(rule)
if calling != null
    . closing = left-call(pattern, rule, List'SyntaxId())
    if closing != 0
        report-left-recursion(closing)
        = invalid-type
    if declared == no-type
        frame.diagnose(left, .stated, program.store-atom("Can't infer return type after recursion"))
        = invalid-type
    for position in calling .. < rules.length
        facts.local-rules[facts.note-local-rule(instance, rules[position])].recursive = true
    = declared
. place = facts.note-local-rule(instance, rule)
rules += rule
typed-rules += rule
typed-helpers += helping.site
. own-arms = rule-arming
. base = capture-sites.length
rule-arming = RuleArms(declared, gives-source-span(declared), true, declared == types.string-type, pattern, base, rule-arming.casting)
. saved-explicit = helping
. saved-unvalued = valuing
helping = helping.explicit = marked || (beside-rule && holds-rollback(pattern))
valuing = valuing.unvalued = false
. joined = arms-type(pattern)
valuing = saved-unvalued
. carried-rolls = helping.rolls
helping = saved-explicit
helping = helping.rolls = carried-rolls
-= capture-sites[base .. < capture-sites.length]
-= capture-slots[base .. < capture-slots.length]
-= capture-accumulating[base .. < capture-accumulating.length]
-= capture-patterns[base .. < capture-patterns.length]
-= capture-repeats[base .. < capture-repeats.length]
rule-arming = own-arms
rules.pop()
if joined == invalid-type
    = invalid-type
. result = declared
if result == no-type
    result = if joined == no-type then types.string-type else joined
convert-stream-arms(pattern, result)
if declared != no-type && declared != types.string-type
    note-arm-casts(pattern, declared)
facts.set-node-type(instance, pattern, result)
facts.set-node-type(instance, matched, result)
facts.local-rules[place].answer = types.optional-around(result)
= result

────────────────────
_ item-holds Bool
    - point U64

` Whether integer items hold a character a pattern tests them against as its code point: one
` their type fits, and over items of a byte, which hold the UTF-8 of text, one that is ASCII.
literal-fits-target(types, IntegerLiteral(point, false, false), stream-view.item) && ascii-or-wide
.. ascii-or-wide = point < 0x80 || types.completion-of(stream-view.item).bit-size > 8

────────────────────
_ bound U64
    - id SyntaxId

` The code point a bound of a range of characters is written as.
match tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-integer-syntax(row)
        parse-integer-literal(row.value).value
    ??
        0

────────────────────
_ char-bound Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a bound of a range of characters is a character written, as the reference requires: a
` character literal, whose unit is `(char)`, or a number with no unit or `Char`'s suffix.
match tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-integer-syntax(row)
        !row.unit || row.unit.text == "(char)" || row.unit.text == "c"
    ??
        false

────────────────────
_ count-bound Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a bound of a count is a number written.
match tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-integer-syntax(row)
        !row.unit
    ??
        false

────────────────────
_ do counts Bool
    - part SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId
    - repeated Bool

` Whether a bound of a count has a shape here, and the error at the bound where it has not: a
` number written, or an integer computed as the match runs. The reference reads the most again
` before each time it takes the part, so a bound it reads more than once must give the same
` each time without doing anything, as `steady` says. A bound is typed once, however often the
` part is.
if count-bound(id)
    = true
. known = facts.node-type(instance, id)
. type = if known != no-type then known else infer(id)
if type == invalid-type || type == no-type
    decline(part)
    = false
if !is-integer-kind(types.intrinsic-of(type))
    . shown = type-display(types, type)
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("A count in a pattern must be an integer, not $shown"))
    = false
if repeated && !steady(id)
    . advice = "compute it in a lazy local with \"..\" and count by its name"
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("A count in a pattern is read each time the part repeats, and this one may change between reads; $advice"))
    = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do steady Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether an expression gives the same each time it is read without doing anything: a name, a
` literal, a constant such as the size of a type, a lazy local or a global, an integer cast to
` another, one of two such picked by such a number or truth, and such numbers or truths
` compared, joined by `&&` or `||`, or added, taken away, multiplied or combined bit by bit,
` which wrap rather than panic.
if is-quiet(id)
    = true
. plan = facts.plan-of(instance, id)
if plan == .plan-constant || plan == .plan-type-size
    = true
do match? tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-identifier
        . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, id)
        if resolution.kind == .resolve-global
            = true
        . slot = capture-slot(id)
        = slot != no-slot && bindings.slots[slot].kind == .slot-lazy
    | .node-cast-expression(row)
        . given = types.intrinsic-of(facts.node-type(instance, row.lhs))
        . made = types.intrinsic-of(facts.node-type(instance, id))
        = is-integer-kind(given) && is-integer-kind(made) && steady(row.lhs)
    | .node-binary-expression(row)
        if row.op == .if-op
            . test = types.intrinsic-of(facts.node-type(instance, row.rhs))
            = (is-integer-kind(test) || test == .bool) && steady(row.lhs) && steady(row.rhs)
        if row.op == .coalesce-op || row.op == .else-op
            = steady(row.lhs) && steady(row.rhs)
        if steady-operator(row.op)
            . left = types.intrinsic-of(facts.node-type(instance, row.lhs))
            . right = types.intrinsic-of(facts.node-type(instance, row.rhs))
            . plain = (is-integer-kind(left) || left == .bool) && (is-integer-kind(right) || right == .bool)
            = plain && steady(row.lhs) && steady(row.rhs)
= false

────────────────────
_ steady-operator Bool
    - op Operator

` Whether an operator on two numbers or truths gives the same each time without doing anything:
` a comparison, `&&` and `||`, and arithmetic that wraps rather than panics.
compares || joins || wraps

.. compares = op == .equals-op || op == .not-equals-op || op == .less-than-op || op == .greater-than-op || op == .less-than-equals-op || op == .greater-than-equals-op
.. joins = op == .and-op || op == .or-op
.. wraps = op == .add-op || op == .subtract-op || op == .multiply-op || op == .bitwise-and-op || op == .bitwise-or-op || op == .bitwise-xor-op

────────────────────
_ do final-raise SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` The raise that always runs that an action ends in, as `?! Oops(1009)` is, or none.
do match? tree.nodes[body]
    | .node-assertion-syntax(row)
        = if row.condition == 0 then body else 0
    | .node-block(row)
        . last SyntaxId = 0
        for statement in tree.children[row.body]
            . lazy = false
            do match? tree.nodes[statement]
                | .node-declare(declaration)
                    lazy = declaration.is-lazy
            if !lazy
                last = statement
        = if last != 0 then final-raise(last) else 0
= 0

────────────────────
+ always-passes Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a stream pattern always gives a value or raises: its last arm has no pattern, or
` raises.
match tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-stream-or(row)
        always-passes(row.right)
    | .node-stream-transform(row)
        row.pattern == 0 || always-passes(row.pattern)
    | .node-stream-panic
        true
    ??
        false

────────────────────
_ do mentions Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - name String

` Whether a name is read anywhere in an expression, as the reference finds what an action
` refers to. An `it` read in the action of an arm written within the expression is that arm's
` own.
if id == 0
    = false
for node in tree.subtree-start(id) .. < id + 1
    do match? tree.nodes[node]
        | .node-identifier(row)
            if row.name.text == name && (name != "it" || !in-inner-action(node, id))
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do in-inner-action Bool
    - node SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a node lies in the action of an arm of a stream pattern written within an expression.
for outer in node + 1 .. < id
    do match? tree.nodes[outer]
        | .node-stream-transform(row)
            if row.right != 0 && tree.subtree-start(row.right) <= node && node <= row.right
                = true
= false
